RF.put("questb:b22",{"8662":{"id":8662,"t":"Doomcaller's Circlet","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Vek'nilash's Circlet, 2 Idols of Death, 5 Silver Scarabs and 5 Bone Scarabs to Andorgos in Ahn'Qiraj. You must also attain Friendly reputation with the Brood of Nozdormu to complete this quest.\nVek'nilash's Circlet Emperor Vek'nilash in Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n2 Idol of Death Vekniss Soldier 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Stinger 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Silver Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Bone Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 3000 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","desc":"The Twin Emperors... their incessant whispers are slowly taking a toll on my sanity. They mock me, knowing I cannot step further into their domain to save my brother Arygos.\nIn my visions I see their monstrous faces adorned by powerful crowns. But I will have my revenge... I will transmute these symbols of Qiraji power to ones better suited to our needs.\nBring me the components I require, ‹name›. I will give you a headpiece of unmatched power.","rew":"You will receive:\nDoomcaller's Circlet\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"Did you bring me the components I asked for, ‹name›?","done":"You've succeeded! The whispers from the Twin Emperors have ceased.\nTake this as a reward. The mere sight of it will strike fear in the hearts of the Qiraji... it shall remind them of their fallen leaders and of the mortal that slew them.\nStart Andorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple End Andorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Both factions Class Warlock Type Raid Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8662\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 16,550 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Mortal Champions\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Doomcaller's Circlet this quest\nBring Vek'nilash's Circlet, 2 Idols of Death, 5 Silver Scarabs and 5 Bone Scarabs to Andorgos in Ahn'Qiraj.\nAndorgos Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n9,950 XP","cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8582":{"id":8582,"t":"The Horde Needs Purple Lotus!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 1 instead of 50.","obj":"Bring 20 Purple Lotus to Apothecary Jezel at the Valley of Spirits in Orgrimmar.\n20 Purple Lotus Elder Torntusk 40 % , Constrictor Vine 1.9 % , Heavy Fel Iron Chest 1.9 % , Adamantite Bound Chest 1.9 % and 4 more","desc":"The purple lotus, ‹class›, is a reagent in a great many potions, elixirs and oils, some of which will be of use to us at Ahn'Qiraj. We're going to need to create an immense number of those potions for the war effort. And I'm going to experiment to find more uses for the lotus as well. But to do all of that I'm going to need a great quantity of the flower.\nThat's where you come in. Go out into the field and collect up as many purple lotuses as you can. Is this something that you are willing to do for us?","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Horde Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","back":"Returned already with the purple lotus that I have requested, ‹class›? It is critical that you do so in as timely as fashion as possible lest all that I am attempting here come to naught.","done":"A commendable effort, ‹class›. I will measure these specimens for their appropriate usage and note your contribution. The purple lotus will then need to be properly stored until I am ready for them. As for you, if you are still available I should imagine that I'll still need more purple lotus. Please check back with me in a moment.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":32.9,"y":68.5,"n":"Apothecary Jezel","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"6982":{"id":6982,"t":"Coldtooth Supplies","lv":55,"min":51,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Level 55 instead of 60. Pays 85s instead of 0.","obj":"Bring 10 Coldtooth Supplies to the Alliance Quartermaster in Dun Baldar.\n10 Coldtooth Supplies Coldtooth Supplies in Alterac Valley","desc":"The Coldtooth mine is a storage depot for the Horde. I can't stomach the food they give their troops, and the state of their arms and armor is atrocious! But... in times like these when supplies are so important, we can use what they have.\nEnter the Coldtooth mine and bring me back their supplies. That will help keep the Alliance in fighting shape, and remove much needed equipment from the Horde's warriors.\nGood luck, ‹name›. The mine is to the distant south, deep in Horde territory.","rew":"Money: 85 0 gold, 85 silver, 0 copper\n+25 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Have you been to the Coldtooth mine, ‹name›? Do you have the supplies I asked for?","done":"Ah, you got them. Good work, ‹name›! These supplies are a little musty from sitting in that dark mine for so long, but we'll make use of them nonetheless.\nThank you, ‹name›. Your deeds are vital to the maintenance of our fighting forces.\nStart Stormpike Quartermaster Alterac Valley End Stormpike Quartermaster Alterac Valley Level 55 , requires level 51 Difficulty 51 53 58 Side Alliance Type PvP Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 6982","cats":["alterac-valley"]},"7302":{"id":7302,"t":"Fallen Sky Lords","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find out what became of Wing Commander Guse, Wing Commander Jeztor, and Wing Commander Mulverick. Return to Commander Mulfort should you complete your mission.\nGuse's Location Discovered\nJeztor's Location Discovered\nMulverick's Location Discovered","desc":"Our air support is in shambles, ‹name›. The Wing Commanders were shot down over enemy territory. You must find out what became of them so that we can attempt a rescue!\nGuse was last seen flying over the Icewing Bunker. Jeztor's War Rider was spotted near the Stormpike lumber mill. Mulverick... that reckless fool was seen crashing near the Dun'Baldar North Bunker.\nThat's all the information I have. Move out! Search through the areas thoroughly.","rew":"Experience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Frostwolf Clan\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Status of the hunt, soldier?","done":"Well done! The information you recovered will be invaluable to our cause.\nStart Commander Mulfort End Commander Mulfort Level 60 , requires level 51 Difficulty 51 56 58 Side Horde Type PvP Shareable Yes Quest ID 7302","cats":["alterac-valley"]},"7222":{"id":7222,"t":"Speak with Voggah Deathgrip","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 650 experience instead of 9,500, 0.07 times as much.","obj":"Speak with Voggah in Frostwolf Keep.","desc":"A ‹class›? Good! We are glad to see you in Alterac, ‹name›. Interloping dwarves and their allies invade our valley, and we welcome all in the Horde to join us in righteous slaughter!\nSpeak with Voggah Deathgrip. He is looking for agents for an important mission into the Alliance's stronghold in Alterac Valley!\nYou will find Voggah in Frostwolf Keep.","rew":"Experience: 650","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":63.8,"y":60.5,"n":"Voggah Deathgrip","e":1}],"cats":["alterac-valley"]},"7142":{"id":7142,"t":"The Battle for Alterac","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays 2g 70s instead of 0.","obj":"Enter Alterac Valley and defeat the dwarven general, Vanndar Stormpike. Then, return to Voggah Deathgrip in the Alterac Mountains.","desc":"The Stormpike dwarves and their allies have invaded Alterac Valley, and we must drive them out! To win the battle for Alterac, we must defeat their general, Vanndar Stormpike!\nYou will find Vanndar in Dun Baldar, in the north of Alterac Valley.\nDestroy him, ‹name›, and then return to me.","rew":"Money: 2 70 2 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Frostwolf Clan\n+200 reputation with Orgrimmar","done":"Well done, ‹name›! Stormpikes have no hope in this foolish invasion.\nHah! So far, all they've done is get their general killed!","pins":[{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":63.8,"y":60.5,"n":"Voggah Deathgrip","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["alterac-valley"]},"8262":{"id":8262,"t":"Arathor Advanced Care Package","lv":60,"min":45,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nArathor Advanced Care Package\nExperience: 650\n+10 reputation with The League of Arathor","done":"You've certainly begun to prove yourself to us, ‹name›. As a reward, please take this care package! Inside it you'll find rations and bandages that are usable only inside Arathi Basin.\nAs you continue to prove yourself inside the Basin, you'll find that these items will become available to you for purchase. Rations become available when you are Honored with us, and bandages when you are Revered.","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":46,"y":45.2,"n":"Samuel Hawke","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-basin"]},"662":{"id":662,"t":"Deep Sea Salvage","lv":40,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"First Mate Nilzlix wants you to retrieve the Charts and Logs from the Maiden's Folly and the Spirit of Silverpine.\nMaiden's Folly Charts Maiden's Folly Charts\nMaiden's Folly Log Maiden's Folly Log\nSpirit of Silverpine Charts Spirit of Silverpine Charts\nSpirit of Silverpine Log Spirit of Silverpine Log","desc":"O'Breen led the ships into the cove. We were certain this is where the treasure could be found. The Harbinger docked safely but as the Maiden's Folly and Spirit of Silverpine approached the tides began to lower. Strangest thing I've ever seen!\nThose two ships ran aground into something... some sort of temple in the reef. They sank so quickly, was quite a tragedy.\nWe need to retrieve their Logs as well as their Charts before we leave. We can't leave that information behind for prying eyes!","rew":"You will receive:\nBlack Water Hammer\nExperience: 3,150\n+100 reputation with Booty Bay\n-500 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","back":"How goes the search and recovery mission, ‹name›? We really need to get those Logs and Charts back from the Maiden's Folly and Spirit of Silverpine.\nIf the information from those sources were to fall into enemy hands, Fleet Master Seahorn would force us down the plank.\nThat is if we ever get out of this mess...","done":"Knowing this information is secure will bring some ease to the command in Booty Bay. Well done, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":32.8,"y":81.5,"n":"First Mate Nilzlix","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"3542":{"id":3542,"t":"Delivery to Andron Gant","lv":52,"min":45,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Tablet of Markri to Andron Gant in Undercity.\nTablet of Markri Tablet of Markri\nProvided: Tablet of Markri","desc":"Andron Gant is my next contact. He usually holds himself up in the Undercity... right near the Apothecarium.\nHe was a little more loose-lipped when it came to speaking about what he wanted the Tablet for. Apparently some of the mages of Undercity are looking to study some of the arcane spells the highborne used. They think this tablet will help them. Markri was adept at summoning creatures; especially elementals.\nTake the Tablet of Markri and return to me for your part of the reward.","rew":"Money: 60 0 gold, 60 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,550","back":"Well... ... isn't this a surprise? An adventurererere... !\nWhat c'n I do for you... ?","done":"Here, take some coin... get yerself... <hic>... some new armor or something....\nThis'll bring a shiny gold or two to the right... <hic> people.\nAzshara Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Azshara","x":22.6,"y":51.4,"n":"Jediga","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":54.8,"y":76.3,"n":"Andron Gant","e":1}],"cats":["azshara"]},"3382":{"id":3382,"t":"A Crew Under Fire","lv":57,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Defend Captain Vanessa Beltis, her crew and the Horizon Scout's passengers against the naga attack. Captain Vanessa Beltis must survive.","desc":"We were just off the coast looking for a safe haven to make anchor. The sun hadn't been down for more than an hour when they attacked... those damned naga!\nI'm not sure what they were looking for, but it's clear they didn't find it--they've already come back once. A couple of my scouts are on watch at the entrance of the valley to give us fair warning when the next attack comes.\nI'm sorry you've come along now, ‹name›, but it's out of my hands.\nAre you ready for the fight of your life?","rew":"Experience: 600","done":"You've done it! Thank you! Surely this was one of the most brutal battles I've ever taken part in. I can't thank you enough.\nI only wish more of my crew could have lived through this trial.\nI would ask you to speak to any surviving passengers from the Horizon Scout. Some of them had business in the area, and may have a request or two of you if you're willing. Again, thank you for all your help.","pins":[{"z":"Azshara","x":53.1,"y":87.8,"n":"Captain Vanessa Beltis","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["azshara"]},"6822":{"id":6822,"t":"The Molten Core","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 55 instead of 57.","obj":"Kill 1 Fire Lord, 1 Molten Giant, 1 Ancient Core Hound and 1 Lava Surger, then return to Duke Hydraxis in Azshara.\nMolten Giant slain\nFirelord slain\nAncient Core Hound slain\nLava Surger slain","desc":"‹name›, perhaps it is time to give you a real test. Are you ready?\nAt the bottom of Blackrock Depths is a passage to the Molten Core. This is a stronghold of our enemy, held by the most powerful servants of fire on this world.\nGo to the Molten Core, ‹name›. Show me you have the strength and the will to defeat what you find there.\nAnd if you have allies among your people, then rally them. Nothing short of an army can hope to enter the Molten Core and live.","rew":"Experience: 9,950","back":"Your success in the Molten Core awaits, ‹name›.","done":"You have done what most of your kind would think impossible. You have faced the beings of the Molten Core, and triumphed!\nFor so small a creature, you have displayed great resource.\nSome day, perhaps we might strike a true allegiance between your kind and the Waterlords.","pins":[{"z":"Azshara","x":79.3,"y":73.7,"n":"Duke Hydraxis","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["azshara"]},"4342":{"id":4342,"t":"Kharan's Tale","lv":59,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Listen as Kharan Mighthammer tells his story.","desc":"Please, hear me out before passing judgement!","rew":"Experience: 1,600","back":"Allow me to finish telling my story.","done":"As you can see, there was nothing I could have done.\nStart Kharan Mighthammer End Kharan Mighthammer Level 59 , requires level 50 Difficulty 50 55 57 Side Alliance Type Dungeon Shareable Yes Quest ID 4342\nThe chain\n4 quests at level 59, 25,700 XP in all.\n1 [ 59 ] Kharan's Tale this quest\nListen as Kharan Mighthammer tells his story.\nKharan Mighthammer\n1,600 XP\n2 [ 59 ] The Bearer of Bad News\nReturn to Ironforge and deliver the bad news to King Magni Bronzebeard.\nKharan Mighthammer\n6,400 XP\n3 [ 59 ] The Fate of the Kingdom\nReturn to Blackrock Depths and rescue Princess Moira Bronzebeard from the evil clutches of Emperor Dagran Thaurissan.\nKing Magni Bronzebeard Dun Morogh\n8,050 XP\n4 [ 59 ] The Princess's Surprise\nReturn to Ironforge and speak with King Magni Bronzebeard.\nPrincess Moira Bronzebeard\n9,650 XP","cats":["blackrock-depths"]},"4262":{"id":4262,"t":"Overmaster Pyron","lv":52,"min":48,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Slay Overmaster Pyron and return to Jalinda Sprig.\nYou recall Jalinda talking about Pyron guarding the quarry. Perhaps you should search there?\nOvermaster Pyron slain","desc":"The last five of my mages that went snooping around in Blackrock Mountain came back extra crispy with a permanent orange gnomefro - or worse.\n<Jalinda picks up some ashes from the ground and releases them into the air.>\nOne nasty bugger in particular, Overmaster Pyron, seems to be causing quite a bit of trouble. We need that elemental terminated so that our expedition crew can make its way into Blackrock Depths!\nHe guards the entrance at the Blackrock Quarry.","rew":"Money: 1 55 1 gold, 55 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,100\n+100 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"<Jalinda appears to be staring at your head.>","done":"Incendius? Oh dear...\nBurning Steppes Searing Gorge","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":85.4,"y":70.1,"n":"Jalinda Sprig","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-mountain"]},"4982":{"id":4982,"t":"Bijou's Belongings","lv":59,"min":55,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Bijou's Belongings and return them to her. You recall her mentioning that she stashed them on the bottom floor of the city.\nBijou's Belongings Bijou's Belongings","desc":"At night when this place is lightly guarded, I sneak around the city, taking notes and writing down anything I see that could be of some strategic value to the K.E.F.\nLast night, however, things went dreadfully wrong. I stumbled across a tripwire and set off an alarm. I stashed my recon gear and ran for cover! Unfortunately, I can't get back to that gear. They've doubled and tripled up the patrols! All that information is lost.\nGet my belongings back and I'll return to the K.E.F. peacefully.","rew":"Experience: 6,400","back":"Any luck?","done":"You've done it! Once Lexlort has these plans, he'll forget all about the nasty things he wanted to do to me.\n‹name›, you're my hero!\nStart Bijou End Bijou Level 59 , requires level 55 Difficulty 55 57 Side Horde Type Dungeon Shareable Yes Quest ID 4982\nThe chain\n3 quests at level 59, 19,200 XP in all.\n1 [ 59 ] Operative Bijou\nTravel to Blackrock Spire and find out what happened to Bijou.\nLexlort Badlands\n6,400 XP\n2 [ 59 ] Bijou's Belongings this quest\nFind Bijou's Belongings and return them to her.\nBijou\n6,400 XP\n3 [ 59 ] Bijou's Reconnaissance Report\nTake Bijou's Reconnaissance Report back to Grandmaster Lexlort in Kargath.\nBijou\n6,400 XP","cats":["blackrock-spire"]},"6502":{"id":6502,"t":"Drakefire Amulet","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 8,300 experience instead of 9,050, 0.92 times as much.","obj":"You must retrieve the Blood of the Black Dragon Champion from General Drakkisath. Drakkisath can be found in his throne room behind the Halls of Ascension in Blackrock Spire.\nBlood of the Black Dragon Champion General Drakkisath","desc":"It is a piece of the dragon; a scale - enchanted and transformed. Whole, it could have granted access to the beast's lair. Shattered, it is useless.\nIt is possible to repair the item, but to do so would require the blood of a black dragon champion. There is one... He is known as General Drakkisath, ruler of the dragonspawn armies of Nefarian. Perhaps you have heard of him?\nReturn with his blood, ‹race›, and I shall enchant the fragment into something that will grant you access to Onyxia's lair.","rew":"You will receive:\nDrakefire Amulet\nExperience: 8,300","back":"The flow of time does not stop or slow, ‹race›. While my life is eternal, yours is not. Waste not the time that you have...","done":"This amulet will grant you the access that you seek. The lair of Onyxia can be found in Dustwallow Marsh. As long as you hold the amulet, her wards cannot prevent you from entering.\nThe Blue Flight wishes you luck, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":54.5,"y":51.2,"n":"Haleh","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-spire"]},"4742":{"id":4742,"t":"Seal of Ascension","lv":60,"min":57,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find the three gemstones of command: The Gemstone of Smolderthorn, Gemstone of Spirestone, and Gemstone of Bloodaxe. Return them, along with the Unadorned Seal of Ascension, to Vaelan.\nThe Generals, as told to you by Vaelan, are: War Master Voone of the Smolderthorn; Highlord Omokk of the Spirestone; and Overlord Wyrmthalak of the Bloodaxe.\nGemstone of Spirestone Highlord Omokk 13 %\nGemstone of Smolderthorn War Master Voone 17 %\nGemstone of Bloodaxe Overlord Wyrmthalak 26 %\nUnadorned Seal of Ascension Bloodaxe Summoner 5 % , Bloodaxe Warmonger 5 % , Bloodaxe Evoker 5 % , Bloodaxe Raider 5 % and 4 more","desc":"As you can see, the unadorned seal has three empty sockets. Each of those sockets must be filled with a gemstone representing the leadership's command. Finally, Overlord Wyrmthalak, master of the lower citadel, must forge the seal in the flames of the Black Dragonflight.\nUnderstand this, mortal: the chance that one of the three generals of the lower citadel would carry a gemstone at any given time is rare. You must be vigilant in your quest. Remain determined!","rew":"Experience: 8,300","back":"Courage and patience above all else, ‹name›!","done":"<Vaelan's image blurs for a moment.>\n<The pieces that you had collected have disappeared.>\nThe Unforged Seal of Ascension is now ready. It is time for the final step.\nStart Vaelan End Vaelan Level 60 , requires level 57 Difficulty 57 58 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Dungeon Shareable Yes Quest ID 4742\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 18,250 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Seal of Ascension this quest\nFind the three gemstones of command: The Gemstone of Smolderthorn, Gemstone of Spirestone, and Gemstone of Bloodaxe.\nVaelan\n8,300 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Seal of Ascension\nTravel to the Wyrmbog in Dustwallow Marsh.\nVaelan\n9,950 XP","cats":["blackrock-spire"]},"5302":{"id":5302,"t":"The Way of the Weaponsmith","lv":40,"min":40,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"To become a Weaponsmith, you must make the following items and return them to Borgosh: 4 Moonsteel Broadswords, 4 Massive Iron Axes, 2 Heavy Mithril Axes, and 2 Big Black Maces.\n4 Moonsteel Broadsword\n4 Massive Iron Axe\n2 Heavy Mithril Axe\n2 Big Black Mace","desc":"One day, I will create a legendary hammer. A hammer fit for a Warchief!\nIt is my life's work, ‹name›. My passion. I recognize that you have the potential to be among us, one of us - a weaponsmith. I am the one that can help you harness that potential.\nA simple task is all that you must complete. Simple for one of your exceptional skill.","rew":"You will learn: Weaponsmith\nExperience: 3,150","back":"For the glory of the Horde!","done":"This is the final step before you begin your new career as a weaponsmith, ‹name›. Should you choose to back out, now would be your last chance. Otherwise, prepare to be consumed by knowledge!","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":79.4,"y":23.7,"n":"Borgosh Corebender","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blacksmithing"]},"2582":{"id":2582,"t":"Rage of Ages","lv":50,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring three Snickerfang Jowls, two Blasted Boar Lungs, and one Scorpok Pincer to Bloodmage Drazial.\n3 Snickerfang Jowl Starving Snickerfang 40 % , Snickerfang Hyena 40 % , Ravage 30 %\n2 Blasted Boar Lung Ashmane Boar 40 % , Helboar 40 % , Grunter 30 %\nScorpok Pincer Scorpok Stinger 40 % , Clack the Reaver 30 %","desc":"Ah, ‹name›, welcome back. It seems you enjoyed the effect of the robust, operational imbue, derived from snickerfang. Be warned, while the immediate effect is a titanic burst of strength, the long term effects on your spirit and intelligence could be hazardous.\nWith that said, do you require more? If so, bring me another three snickerfang jowls, two blasted boar lungs, and one scorpok pincer.","rew":"You will receive:\nR.O.I.D.S.","back":"Do you have the beast organs?","done":"There you go! Remember, use it sparingly. If you require another, come see me after you finish the one you currently have in your possession.","pins":[{"z":"Blasted Lands","x":50.6,"y":14.2,"n":"Bloodmage Drazial","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blasted-lands"]},"4022":{"id":4022,"t":"A Taste of Flame","lv":54,"min":52,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Show Cyrus Therepentous the Black Dragonflight Molt you received from Kalaran Windblade.\nBlack Dragonflight Molt Frenzied Black Drake 96.4 % , Dark Iron Taskmaster 0 % , Heavy War Golem 0 %","desc":"The flight is aware of your work in the Searing Gorge.\nShow it to me, ‹race›. The molt, imbecile.","rew":"Experience: 5,450","back":"<Cyrus's eyes form two blazing spheres.>","done":"<Cyrus examines the molt.>\nYou have proven that you are not entirely useless, mortal.","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":95.1,"y":31.6,"n":"Cyrus Therepentous","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["burning-steppes"]},"4182":{"id":4182,"t":"Dragonkin Menace","lv":54,"min":48,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Slay 15 Black Broodlings, 10 Black Dragonspawn, 4 Black Wyrmkin and 1 Black Drake. Return to Helendis Riverhorn when the task is complete.\nBlack Broodling slain : 0/ 15\nBlack Dragonspawn slain : 0/ 10\nBlack Drake slain\nBlack Wyrmkin slain : 0/ 4","desc":"Life in the Burning Steppes is rife with conflict.\nJust look at this place! We know very little of what happened to these buildings, but we do know that at one time, before the great explosion, this was all part of the Redridge mountain range.\nEnough lamenting! We have a problem, ‹name›. You may have noticed the dragonkin below this ridge. We need assistance in pushing them back. Kill as many as you can and return to me. Succeed and perhaps we can talk of other things.","rew":"Money: 1 65 1 gold, 65 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,450\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"How goes the dragon hunt?","done":"Superb slaying, ‹name›. Now that we know you can handle yourself around dragonkin, we can talk of more pressing matters.","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":85.8,"y":68.9,"n":"Helendis Riverhorn","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["burning-steppes"]},"97942":{"id":97942,"t":"Camping 101 first aid","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Byancie in Dolanaar to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your first aid skill to 20","desc":"So you've taken up First Aid? That's an honorable... and pragmatic pursuit as a ‹class›.\nI reckon I know someone that can teach you how to craft a First Aid Kit for your camp. Injuries are a reality in the world of adventuring and offering some much-needed healing at your camp could even save lives.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own First Aid Kit. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":57.6,"y":56.6,"n":"Lyreena Duskblade","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":55.2,"y":56.8,"n":"Byancie","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"96102":{"id":96102,"t":"Camping 101 tailoring","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Snang in Orgrimmar to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your tailoring skill to 20","desc":"Tailoring is a surprisingly potent tradeskill to invest in, and I'm sure it'll serve you well.\nI know someone that can teach you how to craft a Faction Banner for your camp, provided you have the skill for it. Inspiration and morale are a key part of success on any battlefield, and an inspirational banner can go a long way to keeping you energized.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Rallying Banner. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.\nDurotar Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":52,"y":47.2,"n":"Brakk","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":62.8,"y":49.4,"n":"Snang","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94262":{"id":94262,"t":"Craftsmans writ mana potion","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Mana Potion\nMana Potion","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Mana Potion, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Mana Potion Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94262","cats":["crafting"]},"94342":{"id":94342,"t":"Craftsmans writ tranquil mechanical yeti","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Tranquil Mechanical Yeti\nTranquil Mechanical Yeti","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Tranquil Mechanical Yeti, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Tranquil Mechanical Yeti Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94342","cats":["crafting"]},"7942":{"id":7942,"t":"More Thorium Widgets","lv":60,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"6 Thorium Widget Wildspawn Shadowstalker 0 % , Gordok Warlock 0 % , Thuzadin Shadowcaster 0 % in Stratholme , Blackhand Iron Guard 0 % and 2 more","rew":"You will receive:\n20 Darkmoon Faire Prize Ticket","back":"‹name›, you have been so good to us, bringing me goods without tiring. You have my eternal thanks!\nAlthough our need for Thorium widgets is not as great as it was, you may still bring them to me and I will gladly trade them for Darkmoon Faire tickets.","done":"Here you are, ‹name›. Here are Darkmoon Faire tickets for your enjoyment. Do not, as they say, spend them all in one place!\nMulgore Elwynn Forest","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":38,"y":44.3,"n":"Rinling","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":41.7,"y":70.7,"n":"Rinling","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkmoon-faire"]},"6342":{"id":6342,"t":"Flight to Auberdine","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Ride a hippogryph to Auberdine from the hippogryph master Vesprystus, then bring Nessa's Collection to Laird.\nNessa's Collection\nProvided: Nessa's Collection","desc":"From Rut'theran, there are two methods of travel to Auberdine: by ferry and by hippogryph. Both are quick and reliable, but if you have not yet flown to Auberdine by hippogryph, then I suggest you do.\nIt is sound advice to speak with the hippogryph master in every town that has one. Once you speak to the master, you can then fly there from other towns.\nHere is Nessa's collection. Speak with me again when you are ready to fly to Auberdine and deliver Nessa's collection to Laird.","rew":"Experience: 420\n+50 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Have you come from Teldrassil? Tell me, how is the fishing there?","done":"A package from Nessa? Thank you, ‹name›! She told me she would send me samples of the fish caught near Rut'theran village. She thinks they may be very different from the fish caught here...\nMy! This jawbone is nearly twice the size of the same fish found here. And these scales are as big as a closed fist! Amazing!\nTeldrassil Darkshore","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":58.4,"y":94,"n":"Vesprystus","s":1},{"z":"Darkshore","x":36.8,"y":44.3,"n":"Laird","e":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"982":{"id":982,"t":"Deep Ocean, Vast Sea","lv":17,"min":13,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Murloc-hide Gloves.","obj":"Recover the Silver Dawning's Lockbox and the Mist Veil's Lockbox for Gorbold Steelhand in Auberdine. Both items should be found aboard the wreckage of the ships to the north of the village.\nSilver Dawning's Lockbox Silver Dawning's Lockbox\nMist Veil's Lockbox Mist Veil's Lockbox","desc":"Off the coast of Darkshore to our north are two wrecked ships - the Silver Dawning and the Mist Veil. Some time ago, both ships ran afoul of the blasted murlocs as they sailed across the vast sea into Auberdine. They now lie at the bottom of the ocean as trophies for those fiends.\nBoth captains didn't make it out that night, and their logs and other effects are still below in lockboxes. I'd like for you to recover them for us; it would mean a lot to the crew members still around these parts.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nWelldrip Gloves Noosegrip Gauntlets Murloc-hide Gloves\nNew in Forever: Murloc-hide Gloves.\nMoney: 18 0 gold, 18 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,250\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"The captains of those ships were good night elves, and they deserve a better fate than they were given. Perhaps tending to their personal effects will be the best way to put their spirits to rest.","done":"You've done us here in Auberdine a great service, lad. We'll make sure that their effects are properly taken care of.\nAs for you, please have this. It is the least I can do for someone with the bravery to set things right.","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":38.1,"y":41.2,"n":"Gorbold Steelhand","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"6662":{"id":6662,"t":"Me Brother, Nipsy","lv":12,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Carton of Mystery Meat to Nipsy at the Stormwind Deeprun Tram Depot.\nCarton of Mystery Meat\nProvided: Carton of Mystery Meat","desc":"Me brother, Nipsy, runs a rat kabob operation on the other side of Deeprun. Ye needs to take this here crate o' rats to him before they go bad. Get a move on!\nYe have ridden a tram before, aye? It's easy. Just step aboard when she arrives and enjoy the ride. An' keep yer arms and legs inside durin' the ride, lest ye be peglegged fer life.","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Deeprun Rat Kabob\nMoney: 5 0 gold, 5 silver, 0 copper Experience: 90","back":"<Nipsy puts his index finger through one of the air holes in the carton.>\nAlive and kicking... and just in time!","done":"Poor Monty. Ever since the Gnomeregan incident, he hasn't been the same. That boy has never seen an ocean in his life, let alone being some kind of pirate.\n<Nipsy sighs.>\nAt least he keeps the flow of twitching critters coming.\nStart Monty , an item: Squirrel Token End Nipsy Level 12 , requires level 10 Difficulty 10 15 18 Side Alliance Shareable No Quest ID 6662\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 12, 990 XP in all.\n1 [ 12 ] Deeprun Rat Roundup\nCapture 5 Deeprun Rats by using the Rat Catcher's Flute.\nMonty\n900 XP\n2 [ 12 ] Me Brother, Nipsy this quest\nTake the Carton of Mystery Meat to Nipsy at the Stormwind Deeprun Tram Depot.\nMonty\n90 XP","cats":["deeprun-tram"]},"1382":{"id":1382,"t":"Strange Alliance","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Gain a Friendly reputation with the Gelkis, then speak with Uthek the Wise.\nReach 3000 reputation with Gelkis Clan Centaur","desc":"We are fortunate the centaur clans fight among themselves, for if they joined into a single force then they would be unstoppable. Yes, we are fortunate, and we should press our advantage.\nOne of the centaur clans, the Gelkis clan, is in brutal war with the Magram clan. If we attack the Magram, then perhaps an alliance may be struck with the Gelkis.\nSpeak with Uthek the Wise, in the outskirts of the Gelkis camps in southwestern Desolace. Through her we might strike an alliance with the Gelkis.","rew":"Experience: 2,050\n-500 reputation with Magram Clan Centaur\n+100 reputation with Gelkis Clan Centaur","back":"Be gone! The Gelkis do not want you here. Leave now!!\nReturn after killing many Magram, and then I will speak with you.","done":"Your name is whispered among the Gelkis. You have much Magram blood on your hands. This is good.\nMaybe it is also good if we speak. Speak of what you can do for the Gelkis, and what we can do for you.","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":66.7,"y":10.9,"n":"Captain Pentigast","s":1},{"z":"Desolace","x":36.2,"y":79.2,"n":"Uthek the Wise","e":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"7462":{"id":7462,"t":"The Treasure of the Shen'dralar","lv":60,"min":56,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 650 experience instead of 675, 0.96 times as much.","obj":"Return to the Athenaeum and find the Treasure of the Shen'dralar. Claim your reward!","desc":"In the library, Athenaeum, you will find an ancient chest hidden beneath the stairway. Take from it that which you desire.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBonecrusher Backwood Helm Sedge Boots\nMoney: 2 70 2 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 650","done":"You open the chest to find...\nStart Shen'dralar Ancient End Treasure of the Shen'dralar Level 60 , requires level 56 Difficulty 56 58 Side Alliance Type Dungeon Shareable Yes Quest ID 7462\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 10,600 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] The Madness Within\nYou must destroy the guardians surrounding the 5 Pylons that power the Prison of Immol'thar.\nShen'dralar Ancient\n9,950 XP\n2 [ 60 ] The Treasure of the Shen'dralar this quest\nReturn to the Athenaeum and find the Treasure of the Shen'dralar.\nShen'dralar Ancient\n650 XP","cats":["dire-maul"]},"98342":{"id":98342,"t":"The great cat spirit","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Recover the Relic of the Fang, Relic of the Claw, and Relic of the Silent Shadow from the Stormrage Barrow Den, and return them to the Great Cat Spirit.\nRelic of the Fang\nRelic of the Claw\nRelic of the Silent Shadow","desc":"To draw upon my spirit, you will need more than a few words. To understand and respect my form you must prove that you can embody cunning, stealth, and if you should be cornered, ferocity.\nIn the Barrow Dens just east of here, are three relics of my favor you must acquire. They are guarded by powerful enraged spirits that will attack you on sight. A statue at the entrance will bless you with temporary stealth to get past them.\nReturn these relics to me. We will see if you are ready to take my shape.","back":"Ah, you have returned. I do hope you have brought the relics with you?","done":"Excellent. You have shown you understand the true nature of the cat, and are able to embody the cunning, stealth, and ferocity needed to take my shape.\nI now deem you worthy of my blessing, young ‹class›.","pins":[{"z":"Moonglade","x":54.6,"y":75,"n":"Great Cat Spirit","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"182":{"id":182,"t":"The Troll Cave","lv":4,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Grelin Whitebeard would like you to kill 14 Frostmane Troll Whelps.\nFrostmane Troll Whelp slain : 0/ 14","desc":"My brother Senir and I were sent to different parts of Dun Morogh to investigate the threat posed by the trolls. The Senate has its hands full with the troggs, so they've no need for further annoyances.\nFrom what I've seen, the trolls aren't well situated here in Coldridge Valley--mostly the southern cave. I'd say that the army will not be necessary. A few strong arms should be more than enough.\nPerhaps you'd like to assist in this endeavor? I have the authority to offer compensation for your help.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nAnvilmar Hand Axe Anvilmar Hammer Anvilmar Knife Anvilmar Sledge\nYou will also receive:\n3 Healing Herb\nExperience: 360\n+100 reputation with Ironforge\n+100 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"From what I've learned, these trolls hail from the Frostmane clan. I'm afraid I don't know much else about them that would be of any use to you, ‹name›.","done":"Argh! Those Light-blasted trolls!\n<He takes a few breaths and seems to settle down... a bit.>\nA group of them came in the night and stole my journal! I knew better than to trust that good-for-nothing appr...","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":25.1,"y":75.7,"n":"Grelin Whitebeard","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"96822":{"id":96822,"t":"For honor","lv":6,"min":3,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect the Raider's Battleaxe, Raider's Bow, and Raider's Shield from the Tiragarde Keep outskirts, then return them to Turroc in Razor Hill.\nRaider's Bow\nRaider's Battleaxe\nRaider's Shield","desc":"We lost many brave warriors of the Horde when we sacked Tiragarde Keep. Now that the humans have reinforced the ruins, we cannot collect their remains to properly honor their deaths.\nGo to the ruins surrounding the keep, and search for the weapons left by our fallen kin. We will display them in a place of honor.","rew":"Money: 1 0 gold, 1 silver, 0 copper Experience: 410\n+75 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Have you done what I asked?","done":"These warriors will always be remembered, Ulvarg. You have made sure of that.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":54,"y":42.6,"n":"Turroc","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"262":{"id":262,"t":"The Shadowy Figure","lv":25,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the book you found at Sven's farm and show it to townsfolk in Darkshire.\nBook from Sven's Farm\nProvided: Book from Sven's Farm","desc":"I must know who was that skulker in the shadows I saw the night my family was killed!\nPlease, ‹name›, you have shown your resourcefulness. Please find that shadowy figure. I must learn what secrets he holds!\nI do not have clues that you do not already know, but here - take the book you found at my farm. Perhaps some of the townsfolk can link this book with its owner.","rew":"Experience: 500\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","back":"If you have something that belongs to the shadowy figure for whom you seek, then let me see it. I may be able to divine something of its owner.","done":"Hmm... Someone handled this book recently, someone who is driven by revenge. But the impressions left on it, at least the impressions from the original owner, are faint.\nI can tell, however, that the original owner of this book is not a native of Darkshire.","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":7.8,"y":34.1,"n":"Sven Yorgen","s":1},{"z":"Duskwood","x":75.8,"y":45.3,"n":"Madame Eva","e":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"1222":{"id":1222,"t":"Stinky's Escape","lv":37,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Escort \"Stinky\" Ignatz, then speak with Morgan Stern in Theramore.","desc":"Great, finally something that doesn't want to eat me!\nI need help handling the critters around here, and you fit the mold, buddy/lady.\nThe cook Morgan Stern is researching a new recipe, and he sent me out here to gather bogbean leaves. I guess he thinks they're tasty.\nAnyway, while looking for a bogbean plant... I got myself surrounded! Can you help me out of here, and watch my back as I look for the bogbean?","rew":"You will receive:\nElixir of Lesser Fortitude\nMoney: 40 0 gold, 40 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,850\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Have you seen Mr. Ignatz? I sent him into the swamp some time ago and he hasn't returned!","done":"Mr. Ignatz was just here with the bogbean leaves, and he told me you helped him out of some real trouble.\nThank you, ‹name›. I will ask my uncle to treat you to a feast the next time you visit the Blue Recluse in Stormwind.","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":46.9,"y":17.5,"n":"\"Stinky\" Ignatz","s":1},{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":66.3,"y":45.5,"n":"Morgan Stern","e":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"6582":{"id":6582,"t":"The Test of Skulls, Scryer","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"You must find the blue dragonflight drake champion, Scryer, and slay him. Pry his skull from his corpse and return it to Emberstrife.\nYou know that Scryer can be found in Winterspring.\nThe Skull of Scryer Scryer","desc":"We are Deathwing's children, whelp. Our dominance over the lesser Aspects must be enforced.\nIf you are truly worthy of ascension, the lesser dragonflight will wilt in your presence.\nFind their champions and lay waste to them in the name of our Father!\nTravel to Winterspring and track down the mighty blue drake, Scryer. Crush him and any of the Blue Flight that stand in your path. Tear out his skull and return it to me.","rew":"Experience: 6,600","back":"<Emberstrife hisses.>","done":"One of ssseveral complete...\nDustwallow Marsh Winterspring","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":56.7,"y":87.7,"n":"Emberstrife","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"5142":{"id":5142,"t":"Little Pamela","lv":55,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Pamela Redpath.","desc":"So many of us died at the battle of Darrowshire. So many died... and worse.\nWhen the battle began I hid my niece Pamela, and I do not know what happened to her. I am but a wandering spirit, but my heart still longs to know Pamela's fate.\nPlease, good ‹class›. Will you go to Darrowshire and search for her? It is to the east, beyond Gahrron's Withering.","rew":"Experience: 2,800","done":"Hello. I'm Pamela, what's your name?\nWestern Plaguelands Eastern Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":49.2,"y":78.6,"n":"Marlene Redpath","s":1},{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":31.2,"y":78,"n":"Pamela Redpath","e":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"5542":{"id":5542,"t":"Demon Dogs","lv":56,"min":52,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Slay 20 Plaguehound Runts, 5 Plaguehounds and 5 Frenzied Plaguehounds. Return to Tirion Fordring when the task is complete.\nPlaguehound Runt slain : 0/ 20\nPlaguehound slain : 0/ 5\nFrenzied Plaguehound slain : 0/ 5","desc":"If you are going to remain here, I ask only that you earn your keep. We have many nuisances that could use some 'discipline.'\nYou can start with the Plaguehounds and their runts.\nI cannot offer much in return, but you are guaranteed a warm meal and some conversation should you succeed.","rew":"Experience: 5,800","back":"Do not pity the demon dogs, ‹race›. They are abominations!","done":"Well done, ‹name›. Come. Rest. Let us eat and talk of days long past!","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":5.2,"y":35.6,"n":"Tirion Fordring","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"6022":{"id":6022,"t":"To Kill With Purpose","lv":58,"min":54,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Corin's Crossing to the east and slaughter the Scourge that inhabit the town. Collect 7 pieces of Living Rot in under 10 minutes. Use the Mortar and Pestle to grind the Living Rot into Coagulated Rot.\nCoagulated Rot\nProvided: Mortar and Pestle","desc":"You kill with purpose while you remain on my stead.\nYour first task is to feed my hounds.\nTake this mortar and pestle and travel to Corin's Crossing. Once there, you will find a robust selection of Scourge to slaughter. From their fresh carcasses I need living rot. Take that living rot and grind it up in the mortar, then let it sit to coagulate. Bring the coagulated rot back here.\nAnd imbecile, realize that living rot from the undead doesn't remain 'living' for very long. You must kill quickly!","rew":"Money: 90 0 gold, 90 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,200\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Are you crying? If this is too 'tedious' for you, 'hero,' I recommend that you head back to the Dark Lady and inform her of the horrible mistreatment you received at my farmstead.\nNow get out of my sight!","done":"Disappointing. I was hoping that I'd be feeding you to my hounds, instead.\n<Nathanos sighs.>\nWell, at least you they'll have something to eat.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":22.2,"y":63.5,"n":"Nathanos Blightcaller","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"9142":{"id":9142,"t":"Craftsman's Writ","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Argent Dawn Valor Token","desc":"You know the drill, kid. One valor token gets you a craftsman's writ.","rew":"You will receive:\nSealed Craftsman's Writ\n+10 reputation with Argent Dawn","done":"You earned this, scrub. Now, don't cry about your orders. Fill 'em or destroy 'em.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.3,"y":48,"n":"Dispatch Commander Metz","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"9222":{"id":9222,"t":"Epic Armaments of Battle - Friend of the Dawn","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"For 110 Insignias of the Dawn and 110 Insignias of the Crusade you may choose an item from the Argent Dawn's treasure cache.\n110 Insignia of the Dawn\n110 Insignia of the Crusade","desc":"Greetings, friend. Have you insignias of the Dawn or the Crusade that you would like to redeem for items of great power?\nI must warn you; purchases made at a friendly reputation with the Dawn come with an extremely hefty surcharge. I would advise that you gain a better reputation with the Dawn before moving forward with your plans.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nAmulet of the Dawn Bracers of Hope Bracers of Subterfuge Medallion of the Dawn Talisman of Ascendance The Purifier\n+100 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Choose carefully. There are no refunds.","done":"Good day, ‹name›. It was a pleasure doing business with you.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.8,"y":50.2,"n":"Quartermaster Miranda Breechlock","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"5942":{"id":5942,"t":"Hidden Treasures","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Joseph's Key to Joseph's Chest.\nJoseph's Key\nProvided: Joseph's Key","desc":"Daddy told me to give you this key. He said it opens a chest out back behind the house.\nHe also wanted me to thank you. Did you do a favor for him? Did you tell him you found my doll?\nWell here's the key. And thank you ‹name›. Thank you! You're a very nice man/lady!","rew":"You will receive:\nRing of Protection Archlight Talisman Magebane Scion\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"This chest is old and covered in grime.","done":"The key fits the lock, and the chest opens...","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":31.2,"y":78,"n":"Pamela Redpath","s":1},{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":30.9,"y":77.8,"n":"Joseph's Chest","e":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"4102":{"id":4102,"t":"Cleansing Felwood","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 15 Blood Amber to Maybess Riverbreeze in Felwood.\n15 Blood Amber Dessecus 80 % , Warpwood Shredder 80 % , Warpwood Moss Flayer 80 %","desc":"Plants give life to Felwood, yet even they suffer the taint of corruption. I know ways to cleanse them, but I cannot give out such knowledge to those I don't know or trust. Prove to me that you will truly aid the cause of the Cenarion Circle!\nTo the north lie the Irontree Caverns. The Warpwood elementals present there are now beyond hope of cleansing. I ask you to bring me their sap - blood amber it is called - so I may study it in the hopes of saving other forms of life here.","rew":"Experience: 5,650","back":"I know Felwood suffers, ‹name› - I suffer along with it! I must remain steadfast in my conviction; were the knowledge I possess to fall into the wrong hands, it would spell disaster for all of Felwood.\nBring to me the blood amber drawn from the slain Warpwood elementals, and I will trust you enough to help me enact a means to fight the corruption.","done":"This blood amber will be used to find a means of defeating the corruption present in Felwood. You've proven to me that you're willing to do whatever it takes for the Cenarion Circle. I trust you now, friend.\nIt might seem odd that killing the elementals proved yourself to me, but the end of saving countless sentient beings must justify the means we take. You and I can now focus on the preservation of life through the salves I can make.\n‹name›, the time has come to cleanse Felwood.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":46.7,"y":83.1,"n":"Maybess Riverbreeze","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"2902":{"id":2902,"t":"Woodpaw Investigation","lv":43,"min":39,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find the gnoll battle plans somewhere in the gnoll camps to the south of Camp Mojache.","desc":"Gnolls aren't the sharpest tools in the shed, but they will no doubt have some sort of documented strategy on their recent activity. If we were to find those plans, then we'd have a clearer idea of what is making them so worked up.\nI want you to head back to the Woodpaw and find anything that might resemble their battle plans. They have to have something; their attacks have been too coordinated to be done without them. Find them, and return to me when you have them.","rew":"Experience: 1,800\n+50 reputation with Thunder Bluff","done":"Examining the map reveals it to be the battle plans that Hadoken Swiftstrider wants. Numerous arrows that perhaps represent troop movements are drawn on the map, though most seem to be headed toward the south rather than to the north where Camp Mojache lies.\nAnother section of the map has a picture of what you think is a large insect of some kind, with various tick marks under it. From the looks of the gnolls, it perhaps represents their losses against the unknown bugs...","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":74.9,"y":42.5,"n":"Hadoken Swiftstrider","s":1},{"z":"Feralas","x":71.6,"y":55.9,"n":"Woodpaw Battle Map","e":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"2982":{"id":2982,"t":"The High Wilderness","lv":44,"min":39,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Angelas Moonbreeze wants you to kill 8 Gordunni Warlocks, 8 Gordunni Shaman, and 8 Gordunni Brutes.\nGordunni Warlock slain : 0/ 8\nGordunni Shaman slain : 0/ 8\nGordunni Brute slain : 0/ 8","desc":"Although it is dangerous, Troyas and I have been investigating the ruins that cover the forests of Feralas.\nLately, though, Troyas has been going on his own to the High Wilderness, and I really worry about him. The Gordunni Ogres have taken over that area, and they don't take kindly to anyone that enters their territory.\nI was hoping you might be willing to travel to the ruins to the southeast and clear out some of the ogres. Make it a little safer for my Troyas, and I will be extremely grateful.","rew":"Money: 65 0 gold, 65 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,750\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Be watchful around the Gordunni, ‹name›. Their magic seems to wreak havoc on the very land they stand on.","done":"I am very grateful you were able to do this for me.\nNow, please, don't mention a word to Troyas about this...","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":31.8,"y":45.6,"n":"Angelas Moonbreeze","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"2822":{"id":2822,"t":"The Mark of Quality","lv":46,"min":40,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 Thick Yeti Hides to Jangdor Swiftstrider in Camp Mojache.\n10 Thick Yeti Hide Bloodroar the Stalker 60 % , Lurking Feral Scar 60 % , Enraged Feral Scar 60 % , Hulking Feral Scar 60 % and 1 more","desc":"I take pride in my leather work, and I feel it shows; quality should never be compromised. Anyone who says that quality doesn't matter would also have you believe that the earth does not keep secrets!\nIn my latest pursuit of high-quality materials, I have discovered thick yeti hides. Yetis are native to Feralas, often found west of here in Feral Scar Vale. I'll give you a choice of one of my leather goods for a stack of ten. If that is agreeable to you, then we are set!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nJangdor's Handcrafted Boots Jangdor's Handcrafted Gloves\nExperience: 4,050\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Were you able to get a stack of ten thick yeti hides? My leather goods are second to none, and I'll share a sampling with you should you have the hides.\nIf you can't seem to find yetis, I know where some might be. Try looking west of here, just inland of the Forgotten Coast around the Feral Scar Vale.","done":"Ah, excellent! These hides, when given a special treatment, are as resilient as iron I tell you! It will take many tries in order to get the right mix down for the tanning, but I am confident they will bring my mark of quality to the next level.\nAs for you, ‹name›... your assistance has proven invaluable to me. Please take your choice from these items I have crafted.","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":74.4,"y":42.9,"n":"Jangdor Swiftstrider","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"3062":{"id":3062,"t":"Dark Heart","lv":50,"min":45,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Talo Thornhoof in Camp Mojache wants Edana Hatetalon's Dark Heart.\nEdana's Dark Heart Edana Hatetalon","desc":"Edana Hatetalon is the queen of the Northspring harpies that reside in the ruins to the west. She is pure evil; I have heard that her heart is one of crystal. She is void of any emotion aside from the hate she feels towards all others. You must face Edana and bring me back her dark heart.\nI have heard of a horn that harpies carry -- blowing it by the Hatetalon stones, in the northern part of the ruins, will summon the queen.\nImagine her surprise when it is not her kin calling her, but her death.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nWingcrest Gloves Stronghorn Girdle\nExperience: 5,900\n+150 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"The hate that Edana spreads across the land must be stopped.","done":"Now I know that Edana is truly dead. This heart; I will keep it in memory of what did here for me, ‹name›. Thank you.","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":76.2,"y":43.8,"n":"Talo Thornhoof","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"502":{"id":502,"t":"Elixir of Pain","lv":24,"min":21,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Feed the Elixir of Pain to Stanley.\nElixir of Pain\nProvided: Elixir of Pain","desc":"Ah, nothing like the smell of fresh blood in the foothills!\nNow we'll mix in a touch of this and a little of that and let the real fun begin! What I have created with this blood, I like to call an Elixir of Pain. If my calculations are correct this concoction could be the start of something very beautiful for Lady Sylvanas. But what we need is a test.\nTake this elixir out to the northern farm in Hillsbrad Fields to the southwest. Let's see how Farmer Ray's little dog Stanley likes this \"treat.\"","rew":"Experience: 1,450\n+75 reputation with Undercity","back":"Woof?","done":"You pour some of the elixir into your hand and hold it before Stanley's mouth.","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":61.4,"y":19.1,"n":"Apothecary Lydon","s":1},{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":32.7,"y":35.3,"n":"Stanley","e":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"6102":{"id":6102,"t":"Taming the Beast","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the Taming Rod to tame a Strigid Screecher. Practice your skills, then return the Taming Rod to Dazalar in Dolanaar.\nTaming Rod\nProvided: Taming Rod","desc":"You have tamed two creatures that inhabit the land, now you must tame one that soars the skies. Use the taming rod to tame a strigid screecher, found west of here. Practice your skills with this mighty owl at your side.\nWhen you return, I will bestow you with the skills you will need to tame an animal of your choosing to be your companion; this creature will face the challenges you face, and gain experience alongside you. I will also show you how to call it and dismiss it as you wish.","rew":"You will learn: Taming Lesson\nExperience: 850","back":"I am proud of your accomplishments, ‹name›. Have you finished the last task I gave you?","done":"You have learned all I can teach you, ‹name›. May I offer you one more piece of advice: use discretion when choosing your first pet. Will you choose a creature of the land, of the water, or of the sky? Whatever it may be, without doubt, your pet will be with you for quite some time.\nHere you are, ‹name›. I will now give you the power to tame a beast, as well as call it and dismiss it as you see fit. Use your new skills with pride; you have earned them.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":56.7,"y":59.5,"n":"Dazalar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hunter"]},"9302":{"id":9302,"t":"Missive from the Front","lv":60,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 45 instead of 55.","obj":"Take the Crumpled Missive to the Keeper of the Rolls at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nA Crumpled Missive\nProvided: A Crumpled Missive","desc":"You found this letter on one of the many Scourge minions you've slain. From its appearance and smell, it has been with the undead for some time. Perhaps someone at Light's Hope Chapel would be interested in examining it further...","back":"Yes? What do you have there?","done":"How tragic. These words, clearly meant for someone the soldier loved, never made it to their destination. The events detailed happened years ago; I'm not sure if the intended recipient still lives.\nThere is hope yet, however. With the names and information he gives, I might be able to locate the family! It will take some research, but the librarian in Stormwind owes me a favor...\nThank you for bringing this to me. With your help, we may be able to grant someone peace of mind at least.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.2,"y":50.6,"n":"Keeper of the Rolls","e":1}],"cats":["invasion"]},"3702":{"id":3702,"t":"The Smoldering Ruins of Thaurissan","lv":54,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Listen to Royal Historian Archesonus recant the history of Thaurissan.","desc":"Would you like to hear a brief history of the Dark Iron dwarves?","rew":"Experience: 550\n+10 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Allow me to finish telling you the story of Thaurissan.","done":"Shall we proceed?","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":57.2,"y":30,"n":"Royal Historian Archesonus","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"1942":{"id":1942,"t":"Astral Knot Garment","lv":26,"min":26,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nAstral Knot Robe Astral Knot Blouse\nExperience: 2,100","done":"Your garment is ready! And that silk you gathered was so nice... you don't mind if I made it a little short so that I'd have some silk left over for me, do you?\nI'm only joking. It'll fit you great, and will be perfect for both adventure and formal dining. Enjoy!","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":51.8,"y":83.5,"n":"Wynne Larson","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["mage"]},"90902":{"id":90902,"t":"Rediscovering the light","lv":2,"min":2,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Heal 5 Injured Deathguard with your Holy Light ability.\nInjured Deathguard healed : 0/ 5","desc":"I am proud to welcome another newly risen paladin to our ranks. As you begin to reconnect with the light you may notice that certain abilities that were once second nature to you may cause you considerable pain to use now, particularly those involving channeling the light to heal yourself or others.\nThe only way around this problem is--unfortunately--to go through it. Like any other muscle that has atrophied, you must push through the pain and exercise the flesh for it to return to full function.","back":"Mastery of the light will return, in time.","done":"Pain is nothing new to those who have endured death, and as such the Forsaken are particularly hardy to it. Pain has a purifying property as well that you should embrace as a badge of honor and evidence that you are, in fact, still a servant of the light despite your new circumstances.\nBe well and walk in the light once more, ‹class›.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":31,"y":66.2,"n":"Aramis Hammerhand","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"91862":{"id":91862,"t":"Lumina windsinger","lv":22,"min":18,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Retrieve the Fenris Isle Key from the Rot Hide Gnolls and use it to free Lumina Windsinger.\nFenris Isle Key","desc":"Quel'dorei? No, I am no \"quel'dorei\". I am Lumina Windsinger and I am shen'dorei. One of the Windshaper Skyborne.\nI came to these lands as a guest of the Earthen Ring. My companion Banon and I were passing through Silverpine to reach the Arathi Highlands so that we could study the elemental convergences there. Clearly, we didn't make it.\nWe have no time for this now though. Kill the gnolls nearby. Retrieve the key to this cage and free me. I will tell you the rest once we are safely away.","rew":"Money: 14 0 gold, 14 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,750\n+50 reputation with Undercity\n+100 reputation with Earthen Ring","back":"Gnolls are the second worst creatures I've encountered yet on Azeroth.","done":"Thank you, ‹class›. Unfortunately we aren't out of danger yet.","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":65.6,"y":23.2,"n":"Lumina Windsinger","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"5622":{"id":5622,"t":"In Favor of Elune","lv":4,"min":5,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Laurna Morninglight in Teldrassil.","desc":"‹name›, you must travel to Dolanaar when your business here in Shadowglen is done. There, you will find Laurna Morninglight. She will instruct you further in the ways of Elune, and it is with her that you will earn your first garments denoting your station as a priest/priestess of Elune.\nTake care, and may you be protected in your journeys.","rew":"Experience: 90","done":"I'm happy to see Shanda has sent you to find me, ‹name›. Teaching young priests the ways of Elune gives me great satisfaction.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":59.2,"y":40.4,"n":"Shanda","s":1},{"z":"Teldrassil","x":55.6,"y":56.7,"n":"Laurna Morninglight","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"94822":{"id":94822,"t":"Confounding flash","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak to High Priestess Mims in Ironforge.","desc":"You've caught the attention of our superiors, ‹name›. They've asked you travel to the Hall of Mysteries in Ironforge as soon as possible. Apparently they feel you've proven yourself already and are prepared to further your training. When you get there, find High Priestess Mims. She will be able to guide you further. Good luck, and may the Light be with you.","done":"You took your time arriving, Vall. But you can be excused given your dedicated service to the Light. Please pay close attention to this lesson.\nElwynn Forest Ironforge","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":43.4,"y":65.6,"n":"Priestess Josetta","s":1},{"z":"Ironforge","x":24.8,"y":10,"n":"High Priestess Mims","e":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"7622":{"id":7622,"t":"The Balance of Light and Shadow","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Save 50 Peasants before 15 are slain. Speak with Eris Havenfire should you accomplish this task.\nYou may view the Death Post to view how many Peasants have been slain.","desc":"You must do what I could not: Save the peasants that were cut down while fleeing from Stratholme.\nThey will walk towards the light, you must ensure their survival. Should too many fall, our cursed existence shall continue - you will have failed.\nEvery ability, prayer, and spell that you have learned will be tested. May the Light protect you, ‹name›.","rew":"You will receive:\nSplinter of Nordrassil\nExperience: 9,950","done":"Your tenacity and courage are astounding, priest/priestess. You have earned the right to hold the Splinter of Nordrassil. Only one task remains: The Eye of Shadow must be recovered. Scour the world.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":17.2,"y":12.8,"n":"Eris Havenfire","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"1142":{"id":1142,"t":"Mortality Wanes","lv":30,"min":25,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Sentinel's Boots. Reported by players.","obj":"Find and return Treshala's Pendant to Treshala Fallowbrook in Darnassus.\nTreshala's Pendant Roogug 10 % in Razorfen Kraul , Razorfen Stalker 10 % in Razorfen Kraul , Overlord Ramtusk 10 % in Razorfen Kraul , Charlga Razorflank 10 % in Razorfen Kraul and 4 more","desc":"I have not long to live... so... so... weak.\n...the b-b-brave dwarf, Lonebrow, has been sent to w-w-warn Falfindel...\nBut before I... d-d-die...\n...my wife, Treshala... her pendant of bonding to me... stolen... by one of the f-f-foul aggressors...\nFind it p-p-please... and return it to Treshala in Darnassus...\n...along with w-w-word of my lonely... death.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nMourning Shawl Lancer Boots Sentinel's Boots\nNew in Forever: Sentinel's Boots.\nExperience: 3,050\n+150 reputation with Darnassus","back":"What brings you to my home, ‹race›?","done":"No!\n'Tis not fair. Oh, cruel and intolerable world!\nI must now carry this burden of grief and not let Heralath's work die with him.\nYou were brave to journey from such a dangerous place, ‹name›. But please leave me now.\nIn solitude I shall mourn.","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":69.5,"y":67.8,"n":"Treshala Fallowbrook","e":1}],"cats":["razorfen-kraul"]},"8822":{"id":8822,"t":"Ten Commendation Signets","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"10 Alliance Commendation Signet","back":"I accept commendation signets from adventurers who have received them in the line of duty. For each set of ten that you hand to me, I'll make sure that you receive a significant acknowledgement of your deeds with the Gnomeregan exiles. I also accept single tokens, but at a much reduced rate of recognition. We are much more interested in greater feats of duty, though no feat will be ignored.\nWith that said, I'll gladly take your signets if you are ready to hand in a set.","done":"Excellent! It is no small sacrifice that you've made to earn these signets, and you will be acknowledged for your service appropriately. It's adventurers like you, ‹name›, that truly make a difference.\nLet me know if you have additional signets to hand in; I'll gladly help you out with whatever ones you need exchanged.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":61.2,"y":32.2,"n":"Stormwind Commendation Officer","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.3,"y":28.5,"n":"Officer Porterhouse","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["reputation"]},"92422":{"id":92422,"t":"The Wrath of Rath'mael","lv":22,"min":15,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its experience is what a player got.","obj":"Kill Rath'mael in the Ruins of Lordaeron for Deathguard Kristof in Brill.\nRath'mael slain","desc":"Reports have come in from the Lordamere Overlook deep within the Ruins of Lordaeron. An unholy fog has taken over the streets and graveyard, affording the scourge up there some measure of stealth.\nOur scouts indicate they're being conjured by a new power within their ranks, a necromancer known as Rath'mael. We do not have the luxury of waiting this one out, ‹name›.\nIf you have allies, summon them and their aid to the Forsaken. Drive this creature out of our lands.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nForsaken Greataxe Gnarled Necromancer's Staff\nExperience: 4,600\n+150 reputation with Undercity","done":"While I have no doubt something of his kind will be replaced, we can only hope their ranks thin in the meantime.\nThank you Dead.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":65.2,"y":60.2,"n":"Deathguard Kristof","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ruins-of-lordaeron-dungeon"]},"5382":{"id":5382,"t":"Doctor Theolen Krastinov, the Butcher","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Doctor Theolen Krastinov inside the Scholomance. Destroy him, then burn the Remains of Eva Sarkhoff and the Remains of Lucien Sarkhoff. Return to Eva Sarkhoff when the task is complete.\nDoctor Theolen Krastinov slain in Scholomance\nRemains of Eva Sarkhoff Burned in Scholomance\nRemains of Lucien Sarkhoff Burned in Scholomance","desc":"Krastinov is responsible for the deaths of thousands. He must be punished, justice must be meted out.\nFind him and exact upon him the agony he has inflicted upon countless innocents. Once he is destroyed, burn our remains. Turn them to ashes, ‹name›.","rew":"Experience: 6,600","back":"The Butcher must be stopped!","done":"I can feel my spirit healing, ‹name›. You have done my husband and I a great service, but I am certain there is more to be done.","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":70.2,"y":73.7,"n":"Eva Sarkhoff","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["scholomance"]},"3462":{"id":3462,"t":"Squire Maltrake","lv":50,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Squire Maltrake.","desc":"Speak with my envoy, Squire Maltrake. He will further instruct you as to the use of the Torch of Retribution.","rew":"Experience: 470","done":"Are you prepared to make your strike?","pins":[{"z":"Searing Gorge","x":39.1,"y":39,"n":"Kalaran Windblade","s":1},{"z":"Searing Gorge","x":39.2,"y":39,"n":"Squire Maltrake","e":1}],"cats":["searing-gorge"]},"8902":{"id":8902,"t":"Dearest Elenia,","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver the Lovingly Composed Letter to Elenia Haydon near the bank in the Undercity.\nLovingly Composed Letter\nProvided: Lovingly Composed Letter","desc":"A lifetime ago, I was betrothed to marry Elenia, my childhood sweetheart. It's been years since I thought about her last, but of late, she frequently occupies my thoughts.\nPerhaps, even with everything that has passed, there can be some room in each other's lives for our love.\nI'm sure she has changed, also. Can you deliver this letter to her for me? I am too nervous to give it in person.","back":"Oh, and to what do I owe this pleasure?","done":"This brings back memories from a lifetime ago, ‹name›. Elenia Tor. That was going to be my name, you know. We would have a beautiful ceremony out on the shores of the lake. When he retired, we'd find a farm to retire to.\nSimple dreams, then.\nBut if he saw me now, I doubt he'd even see Elenia in me. Only cold flesh and a dead heart...\nTirisfal Glades Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":60.7,"y":59.5,"n":"Deathguard Tor","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":66.9,"y":45.2,"n":"Elenia Haydon","e":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"7062":{"id":7062,"t":"The Reason for the Season","lv":60,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Historian Karnik at the Explorer's League in Ironforge about the Feast of Winter Veil.","desc":"Gifts, treats, presents... bah, I say!\nThose goblins pollute the true meaning of this season - the Feast of Winter Veil. This is a time of renewal; the land slumbers under a blanket of snow brought forth by Greatfather Winter, who is NOT the bumbling fool over there in the red suit!\nIf you're interested in learning what the Feast is all about for yourself, ask Historian Karnik at the Explorer's League. I'm sure he'll be surprised that someone cares about history rather than getting presents.","rew":"Experience: 650","done":"The Feast of Winter Veil, you say? Alas, in times past it held a more substantial meaning to us dwarves. Nowadays, it seems as though others have turned the legend of Greatfather Winter into something that helps to sell candies and presents.\nIt's no surprise that Goli is bitter about that sort of change. He and other dwarves like him cling to our past like a banner of war. While I think a little celebration is always good, it is important to remember the origins of the Feast.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":55.9,"y":30.6,"n":"Goli Krumn","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":63.5,"y":23,"n":"Historian Karnik","e":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"8982":{"id":8982,"t":"Tracing the Source","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Innkeeper Norman in the Undercity.","desc":"We must find who the supplier is. I noticed Apothecary Katrina with a bottle of the perfume tucked in her pack. She told me that she purchased it from Norman, the innkeeper.","done":"Ah yes, I just recently received stock of the perfume and cologne. I don't know how long I can keep it on the shelves - seems like no one can get enough of it.\nIf you ask me, I don't see what the big deal is.","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":66.7,"y":44.7,"n":"Fenstad Argyle","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":67.7,"y":37.9,"n":"Innkeeper Norman","e":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"1462":{"id":1462,"t":"Earth Sapta","lv":4,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Seer Ravenfeather for another Earth Sapta.","rew":"You will receive:\nEarth Sapta","done":"Take this and remember, it is sacred.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":44.3,"y":76.8,"n":"Seer Ravenfeather","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"94502":{"id":94502,"t":"Call of water","lv":23,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Cleanse the corruption at Stendel's Pond in Westfall.\nReturn to Norric in Loch Modan when finished.\nCorrupt Manifestation's Bracers\nProvided: Remaining Drops of Purest Water","desc":"In Westfall, outside o' Moonbrook lies Stendel's Pond. Once a pure spring, now touched by dark forces. The spirits there 'ave gone silent.\nYe must face the corruption that fouls the waters. Take its bracers and the last drops o' Hervdana's potion, then place 'em on the shrine. That'll call forth a spirit, cleansed and true. Speak with it, learn what ye can.\nBring me proof the deed's done, and I'll grant ye the totem.","back":"The shrine stands aged and forgotten, cloaked in dust and cobwebs. The pond beside it lies eerily still, its surface untouched by wind or life. Scattered along the shore are the bones of beasts once burdened by labor. The water's murky sheen raises a troubling question--has it been poisoned by the surrounding malaise, or is it the very source of it?","done":"You place the bracers atop the shrine and then pour the remaining drops of Norric's potion into dry stone. You begin to incant the simple words Norric taught you and the droplets vaporize atop the stone within the bindings....\nLoch Modan Westfall","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":41.8,"y":19,"n":"Norric Lochthane","s":1},{"z":"Westfall","x":45.6,"y":59.9,"n":"Forgotten Shrine","e":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"93062":{"id":93062,"t":"Bone burying","lv":42,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Maintain your reputation with the Gelkis Clan, and dispel the curses from 8 failed summons throughout the Valley of Bones.\nHaggard Bones laid to rest : 0/ 8\nGelkis Clan Centaur","desc":"About this staff of yours. I recognize it as one of Uthek's, and you mentioned it was constructed with Theradras' Tears, augmented with a Draenethyst Crystal, and that it can dispel dark magic?\nI noticed that there are skeletons stuck just underneath the rocky soil further into the valley. I believe these are failed summons from the Outcast Necromancers, doomed perhaps forever to an existence smothered in dirt.\nLaying them to rest again would be good for our cause, and their spirits.\nLevel 42 , requires level 35 Difficulty 35 38 40 45 53 Side Both factions Quest ID 93062\nThe chain\n3 quests from level 42 to 43, 7,260 XP in all.\n1 [ 42 ] Bone Burying this quest\nMaintain your reputation with the Gelkis Clan, and dispel the curses from 8 failed summons throughout the Valley of Bones.\n3,450 XP\n2 [ 43 ] Checking Things Out\nMaintain your reputation with the Gelkis, and investigate centaur points of interest within Shen'dralas.\n360 XP\n3 [ 42 ] Khan Jehn\nMaintain your reputation with the Gelkis, and slay Khan Jhen at Magram Village.\n3,450 XP","cats":["shendralas"]},"8502":{"id":8502,"t":"Target: Hive'Ashi Workers","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Slay 30 Hive'Ashi Workers and report back to Commander Mar'alith at Cenarion Hold in Silithus. You must also bring Combat Task Briefing III in order to complete this quest.\nCombat Task Briefing III\nHive'Ashi Worker slain : 0/ 30\nProvided: Combat Task Briefing III","desc":"As the war effort mounts, the silithid presence in the area presents an ever increasing threat to our operations. You've been selected to partake on an assault on Hive'Ashi where your primary target will consist of Hive'Ashi workers.\nReport back to Commander Mar'alith after your task is completed.","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Combat Badge\nExperience: 650\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"You have something to tell me, ‹class›?","done":"Excellent work, ‹name›. Without their workers, the silithid will have a hard time repairing any damage inflicted to their hive's structure.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":49.2,"y":34.2,"n":"Commander Mar'alith","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"8342":{"id":8342,"t":"Twilight Ring of Lordship","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"3 Abyssal Signet The Duke of Cynders , The Duke of Fathoms , The Duke of Shards , The Duke of Zephyrs\n5 Large Brilliant Shard","rew":"You will receive:\nTwilight Cultist Ring of Lordship","back":"‹name›, if you plan to go after the Abyssal High Council again, then you'll need another Twilight ring of lordship. Bring me more shards and signets and I'll make one for you.","done":"Ah, I see your convictions are strong. Not many will face that council of fiends!\nHere's your ring, ‹name›. May your will, and your fortune, stand firm.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":52,"y":38.2,"n":"Aurel Goldleaf","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"422":{"id":422,"t":"Arugal's Folly","lv":11,"min":12,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Retrieve the Remedy of Arugal for Dalar Dawnweaver at the Sepulcher.\nRemedy of Arugal Dusty Spellbooks","desc":"How Arugal gained acceptance within the Kirin Tor is beyond me. His spell-casting knowledge seemed as transparent as a blown glass bauble.\nWhat's important now is learning exactly what magic Arugal used so that I can turn it against him and secure Silverpine Forest for the Dark Lady.\nArugal first stayed at the wheat farm just north of the bridge. One of the Deathstalkers reported seeing some spellbooks but could not secure them. Retrieve for me the spell labeled Remedy of Arugal from those books.","rew":"Experience: 875\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Before I know what we are dealing with here, ‹class›, I need to study the spell known as Remedy of Arugal. Bring it to me now or I shall be forced to find myself a worthy servant.","done":"This is precisely the spell I was in search of, ‹class›. If your dedication to The Dark Lady's cause remains infallible you will find you have quite a future amongst The Forsaken.","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":44.2,"y":39.8,"n":"Dalar Dawnweaver","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silverpine-forest"]},"4822":{"id":4822,"t":"You Scream, I Scream...","lv":60,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Get some Strawberry Ice Cream for your ward. The lad seems to prefer Tigule and Foror's brand ice cream.\nTigule's Strawberry Ice Cream sold by Brivelthwerp , sold by Alowicious Czervik , sold by Emmithue Smails , sold by Katrina Shimmerstar and 1 more","desc":"ICE CREAM! Oh please please please could you get me some ice cream?! Strawberry is my favorite flavor, and there's no better strawberry ice cream in the world than Tigule and Foror's Strawberry Ice Cream! It's my favorite ice cream in the whole wide world!\nI had it once a long time ago when I was at the Shimmering Flats race track, but I heard that they might be selling them in town now! Please? Pretty please? With Tigule and Foror's Strawberry Ice Cream on top??!?!","rew":"Experience: 650\n+75 reputation with Alliance","back":"I wish they'd make more flavors of ice cream other than strawberry, but I guess I'm lucky that strawberry is my favorite!","done":"Mmmmmmmmm! I love their strawberry ice cream! If there's one thing Tigule knows how to do, it's make ice cream!\nThank you very much ‹name› - this is the best treat ever!\nStart Human Orphan End Human Orphan Level 60 , requires level 10 Difficulty 10 56 58 Side Alliance Shareable No Quest ID 4822\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 2,300 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] You Scream, I Scream... this quest\nGet some Strawberry Ice Cream for your ward.\nHuman Orphan\n650 XP\n2 [ 60 ] A Warden of the Alliance\nReturn your ward to the Stormwind orphanage by handing in the Human Orphan Whistle to Orphan Matron Nightingale in the Cathedral District.\nHuman Orphan\n1,650 XP","cats":["special"]},"1062":{"id":1062,"t":"Goblin Invaders","lv":19,"min":13,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 15 Venture Co. Loggers, then return to Seereth Stonebreak on the border of Stonetalon and the Barrens.\nVenture Co. Logger slain : 0/ 15","desc":"The goblin-run Venture Company moved into the Stonetalon Mountains, chopping down trees and burning huge stretches of forest. The spirits of this place are nearly blind with pain and rage. We must stop the Venture Company!\nHead northwest, beyond the Greatwood Vale and into the Windshear Crag. You will find the goblins and their servants at work--show them the Horde will not allow the exploitation of Stonetalon. Show them in the language they best understand...\nViolence.","rew":"Money: 11 0 gold, 11 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,450\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"The Greatwood Vale lies to the northwest, ‹name›. Go. Strike fear into those who would pillage this land!","done":"Bravely done, ‹name›.\nWe may ultimately need the wisdom of tauren elders to calm the spirits of Stonetalon, but...\nRidding the Venture Company of its personnel is a good first move against them.\nThe Barrens Stonetalon Mountains","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":35.3,"y":27.9,"n":"Seereth Stonebreak","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"97222":{"id":97222,"t":"Gatehouse goods","lv":15,"min":9,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Carry the Gatehouse Shipment up the stairs in Trias' shop and leave it outside the door.\nGatehouse Shipment delivered","desc":"Yes, it's only a flight of stairs, but if it's such a small ask, it should be no problem for you to finish the delivery yourself!\nTrias' Cheese isn't part of the Gatehouse or their stocking inventory, but our buildings share a floor.\nPlace the crate outside their stockroom door--the guard will send someone for a regular pickup. They will see the package arrival and carry it inside as they return to post.","rew":"You will receive:\n2 Dalaran Sharp\nExperience: 800","done":"Yep. There's a reason that hinge opens inwards towards them, so they don't get the door blocked by people leaving stuff anywhere they please.\nConsider us professionally acquainted, ‹class›.\nWe respect your business, and expect you to respect ours.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":60.4,"y":63.4,"n":"Elaine Trias","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"6182":{"id":6182,"t":"The First and the Last","lv":60,"min":56,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Mathias Shaw in Old Town Stormwind. He resides in the Barracks.","desc":"Nathanos Marris was the first and last of the human ranger lords. A disciple of Sylvanas Windrunner, now the Banshee Queen of the Forsaken.\nWe had thought that Nathanos had been killed in action in the defense of Lordaeron five years ago. Although his corpse was never recovered, it was assumed that he did not make it out of the Eastern Plaguelands.\nMathias Shaw has been investigating the disappearance and may have some new information. Report to him at once. He resides in Old Town, at the Barracks.","rew":"Experience: 650","done":"After some reports of unusual Forsaken activity in the Eastern Plaguelands, SI:7 agents were dispatched to investigate. The results of that investigation are unsettling.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":80.2,"y":38.3,"n":"Highlord Bolvar Fordragon","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":78.3,"y":70.7,"n":"Master Mathias Shaw","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"7782":{"id":7782,"t":"The Lord of Blackrock","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Venture to the Valley of Heroes in Stormwind City and speak with Field Marshal Afrasiabi.","desc":"Go to the Valley of Heroes and speak with Field Marshal Afrasiabi.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nMaster Dragonslayer's Medallion Master Dragonslayer's Orb Master Dragonslayer's Ring\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Stormwind\n+200 reputation with Ironforge\n+200 reputation with Darnassus\n+200 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","done":"<Field Marshal Afrasiabi bows.>\nChoose your reward, let the celebration begin!","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":80.2,"y":38.3,"n":"Highlord Bolvar Fordragon","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":71.5,"y":80.5,"n":"Field Marshal Afrasiabi","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"582":{"id":582,"t":"Headhunting","lv":37,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 20 Shrunken Heads to Nimboya at the Grom'gol Base Camp.\n20 Shrunken Head Bloodscalp Headhunter 80 %","desc":"We must find if Yenniku is dead.\nSlay the Bloodscalp Headhunters and take from them their Shrunken Heads. You must gather many, many heads, and I will inspect them to make sure Yenniku's head is not among them.\nAnd if Yenniku was killed by the Bloodscalps, then may a 600-year curse fall on the spirit of their chief, Gan'zulah!\nGo, ‹name›. You may find many Headhunters at the ruins of Zuuldaia and Zul'Kunda, along the coast to the north.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nDarkspear Cuffs Darkspear Armsplints\nExperience: 2,100\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"‹name›. I fear for our chief's son. Do you have the shrunken heads so I may inspect them?","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. I will inspect these heads to ensure poor Yenniku was spared the headhunter's axe.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":32.2,"y":27.7,"n":"Nimboya","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"342":{"id":342,"t":"Chapter IV","lv":40,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring pages 25, 26, and 27 of Nesingwary's The Green Hills of Stranglethorn to Barnil Stonepot in order to complete Chapter IV.\nGreen Hills of Stranglethorn - Page 25 Lord Sakrasis 2.3 % , Verifonix 2.2 % , Sergeant Malthus 1.9 % , Murkgill Lord 1.5 % and 4 more\nGreen Hills of Stranglethorn - Page 26 Bookie Herod 3.2 % , Mok'rash 2.1 % , Saltscale Oracle 1.4 % , Venture Co. Workboss 1.2 % and 4 more\nGreen Hills of Stranglethorn - Page 27 Mosh'Ogg Butcher 9.3 % , Gluggle 3 % , Negolash 2.4 % , Mok'rash 1.8 % and 4 more","desc":"Ah Chapter IV; the big finale! And what an ending it was!\nWe are only missing three pages for this chapter. We need pages 25, 26 and 27 to put Chapter IV back together.","rew":"You will receive:\nGreen Hills of Stranglethorn - Chapter IV\nExperience: 775","back":"We just need three pages to finish off Chapter IV, ‹name›. Do you have pages 25, 26 or 27 yet?","done":"Superb! We now have Chapter IV ready to go!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":35.7,"y":10.5,"n":"Barnil Stonepot","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"2662":{"id":2662,"t":"Noggenfogger Elixir","lv":49,"min":44,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Marin Noggenfogger wants you to speak to him again after he creates his elixir.","desc":"Now, to mix this powder in with the dew.\nCome back and talk to me in a minute... after I have perfected the fabulous Noggenfogger Elixir!","rew":"You will receive:\n5 Noggenfogger Elixir\nMoney: 70 0 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper","done":"Drink this! It's absolutely wonderful!!!\nI knew I had it in me... Oh thanks again, ‹name› for your help, but please, stand a little to the side, will you? You're blocking my business! I'm going to make millions on the fabulous Noggenfogger Elixir, millions!\nWhat's that? Sprinkle says I owe her a favor? Oh, that Sprinkle, such a kidder!","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":51.8,"y":28.7,"n":"Marin Noggenfogger","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"8182":{"id":8182,"t":"The Hand of Rastakhan","lv":58,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Molthor in Stranglethorn.","desc":"‹name›, our worst fears have come. Legend speaks of the Soulflayer ruling the ancient troll world through evil and terror, and his power was absolute. If he cannot be stopped now, then his new reign may spread across all of Azeroth!\nThere is a contingent of Zandalarian trolls who may help us stem this tide of darkness. They have camped on Yojamba Isle, off the coast of Stranglethorn, west of the ruins of Zul'Kunda. Speak with their leader, Molthor, and pray he knows how to defeat Hakkar.","rew":"Experience: 9,300","done":"You were sent by the prospector, Ironboot? His kind are wise, and wiser still to bring you to me, for I and the Zandalarian trolls may know a way to defeat the Soulflayer.\nSpeak with the trolls of this isle, heed their words, and prepare yourself, ‹name›, for the task before you is soaked in blood.\nTanaris Stranglethorn Vale","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":66.9,"y":24,"n":"Prospector Ironboot","s":1},{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15,"y":15.1,"n":"Molthor","e":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"8742":{"id":8742,"t":"The Might of Kalimdor","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","desc":"A thousand years has passed and just as it was fated, one stands before me. One who shall lead their people to a new age.\nThe Old God trembles, ‹name›. Oh yes, it fears your faith. Shatter the prophecy of C'Thun.\nIt knows you come, champion - and with you comes the might of Kalimdor. You have only to let me know when you are prepared and I shall grant you The Scepter of the Shifting Sands.","rew":"You will learn: Call Scepter DND\nExperience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu\n+200 reputation with Cenarion Circle","done":"The Scepter of the Shifting Sands is whole once more, ‹name›.\nIt must be you who uses the scepter. It must be you who heralds the next age of your people. You must wait for the armies of the Horde and the Alliance to arrive in Silithus before you may ring the Scarab Gong.","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":65.3,"y":50,"n":"Anachronos","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tanaris"]},"902":{"id":902,"t":"Samophlange","lv":16,"min":10,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return the Samophlange to Sputtervalve in Ratchet.\nSamophlange\nProvided: Samophlange","desc":"Pulling open the face of the control console reveals a dense jumble of wires, tubing and other strange mechanical objects--most of which seem to serve no practical purpose. Pushing them aside and digging deeper into the console, you find the samophlange. A tug removes it from its housing.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nEngineer's Hammer Welding Shield\nExperience: 1,150\n+100 reputation with Ratchet","back":"Oh, you're back, ‹name›! Do you have the samophlange?","done":"This is... er... interesting... yes. I'll have it sent along to the Tinkers' Union headquarters in Undermine. I'm sure after some careful dissection and research, they'll be able to make some sense of it.\nBut, perhaps I'll have a little look myself first...","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":52.4,"y":11.6,"n":"Control Console","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":63,"y":37.2,"n":"Sputtervalve","e":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"822":{"id":822,"t":"Chen's Empty Keg","lv":24,"min":11,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 5 Lightning Glands, 1 Thunderhawk Saliva Gland and 1 Kodo Liver to Brewmaster Drohn in Ratchet.\n5 Lightning Gland Stormhide 50 %\nThunderhawk Saliva Gland Greater Thunderhawk 80 %\nKodo Liver Lost Barrens Kodo 80 % , Greater Barrens Kodo 80 % , Barrens Kodo 80 % , Wooly Kodo 80 % and 2 more","desc":"Good stuff, that stormstout, huh?\nI have another recipe that I learned from Chen. Would you be interested? It won't take long to make, and it might be useful if you plan on adventuring some more.\nBring me 5 lightning glands from any stormhide, 1 thunderhawk saliva gland from greater thunderhawks, and a kodo liver from any of the Barrens' kodos.\nLike I said, this stuff has kick; it's the trogg ale that I mentioned to you before.","rew":"You will receive:\n5 Trogg Brew\nExperience: 975\n+50 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"You working hard at finding those ingredients, ‹name›?","done":"Haha! I knew you couldn't resist some of this brew. Come back again anytime you want some more, ‹name›. Just bring me more of the ingredients I had you collect.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.3,"y":38.4,"n":"Brewmaster Drohn","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"2742":{"id":2742,"t":"Rin'ji is Trapped!","lv":47,"min":42,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Escort Rin'ji out of the Quel'Danil Lodge, then find his hidden secret at the Overlook Cliffs to the east.","desc":"Hey ‹race›!\nRin'ji lost axe and was captured! Please, help Rin'ji escape. Me know that ‹race› like you don't like Rin'ji's kind, but Rin'ji begs! Must get out of here!\nGot something for nice ‹race› if he helps Rin'ji out of here/she helps Rin'ji out of here...\nRin'ji is hiding something secret at the Overlook Cliffs.","rew":"Experience: 4,200\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Rin'ji is scared!","done":"This troll tablet must be the \"secret\" that Rin'ji was talking about.\nCovered with strange markings, you can not decipher what the tablet says.\nOran Snakewrithe sent you to this area in the first place... Perhaps he might be able to tell you more about it.","pins":[{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":30.7,"y":46.9,"n":"Rin'ji","s":1},{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":86.3,"y":59,"n":"Rin'ji's Secret","e":1}],"cats":["the-hinterlands"]},"7862":{"id":7862,"t":"Job Opening: Guard Captain of Revantusk Village","lv":51,"min":46,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays 2g 25s instead of 75s.","obj":"You have been tasked with the decimation of 20 Vilebranch Berserkers, 20 Vilebranch Shadow Hunters, 20 Vilebranch Blood Drinkers, and 20 Vilebranch Soul Eaters.\nShould you complete this task, return to Primal Torntusk at Revantusk Village in the Hinterlands.\nVilebranch Berserker slain : 0/ 20\nVilebranch Shadow Hunter slain : 0/ 20\nVilebranch Blood Drinker slain : 0/ 20\nVilebranch Soul Eater slain : 0/ 20","desc":"With the loss of Guard Captain Malkhor, the position of Guard Captain of Revantusk is once again open. If you are interested in becoming Captain of the Guard for Revantusk, complete the following tasks and submit your application to Primal Torntusk:\nExterminate Vilebranch Berserkers.\nExterminate Vilebranch Shadow Hunters.\nExterminate Vilebranch Blood Drinkers.\nExterminate Vilebranch Soul Eaters.","rew":"You will receive:\nRune of the Guard Captain\nMoney: 2 25 2 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,100\n+200 reputation with Revantusk Trolls","back":"Are you here about the job opening?","done":"You are indeed a worthy candidate for the new position, ‹name›. Accept this trinket as a token of our appreciation for your hard work. I will be reviewing all applications next year.","pins":[{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":79.1,"y":79,"n":"Call to Arms!","s":1},{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":78.2,"y":81.2,"n":"Primal Torntusk","e":1}],"cats":["the-hinterlands"]},"5062":{"id":5062,"t":"Sacred Fire","lv":27,"min":24,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Gather 10 bushels of Incendia Agave, and then consult Magatha Grimtotem on Elder Rise in Thunderbluff.\n10 Incendia Agave Incendia Agave","desc":"Arikara is a deadly creature that must be dealt with swiftly. In order to hunt her down you will need to light the sacred fire of life - this will summon Arikara.\nGo now and harvest the rare Incendia agave plant. Once you have harvested enough agave, seek council with Magatha Grimtotem on Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff. She is a powerful shaman that can enchant the agave plant to create a powder that will light the fire.\nTravel northeast to the Boiling Pool and gather Incendia Agave.","rew":"Money: 22 0 gold, 22 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,200","back":"So, Motega Firemain sends word of Arikara...well now that is grave news.\nArikara is a deadly creature born only to seek vengeance against those who have committed heinous acts.","done":"Good, you have gathered the essential amount of Incendia agave. This rare herb found only in Thousand Needles will help light the dormant sacred fire of life.\n<Magatha begins to enchant the Incendia agave.>\nThousand Needles Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":21.5,"y":32.3,"n":"Motega Firemane","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":69.9,"y":30.9,"n":"Magatha Grimtotem","e":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"742":{"id":742,"t":"The Ashenvale Hunt","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Senani Thunderheart at Splintertree Post, Ashenvale.","desc":"Attention, young adventurers! The wilds of Ashenvale await you!\nThe Horde has established a strong presence in the lands north of the Barrens. Our two outposts - Splintertree Post and the Zoram Strand Outpost - strive to bring glory to the Horde! Those who would prove themselves should seek out guidance there. Of note: Senani Thunderheart in Splintertree Post, directly north of the Barrens, seeks adventurers willing to take part in a great hunt of Ashenvale!","rew":"Experience: 160\n+10 reputation with Thunder Bluff","done":"Welcome to the new frontier, ‹name›. Ashenvale is a land of opportunity, one where a young ‹class› like yourself is able to find boundless chances to prove their mettle. Look around the outpost here, and be sure to travel out to the Zoram Strand, as the Horde has another outpost there as well.\nYour presence here tells me that you've come to learn more about the hunt. Listen close, and I will gladly share with you what you need to know.\nThunder Bluff Ashenvale","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":44.3,"y":58.8,"n":"Bluff Runner Windstrider","s":1},{"z":"Ashenvale","x":73.8,"y":61.5,"n":"Senani Thunderheart","e":1}],"cats":["thunder-bluff"]},"3782":{"id":3782,"t":"Morrowgrain Research","lv":50,"min":47,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Seed Voucher to Bashana Runetotem in Thunder Bluff.\nSeed Voucher\nProvided: Seed Voucher","desc":"With what we call an Evergreen Pouch, we have cultivated Tharlendris seeds in the soil from Un'Goro Crater. These seeds have blossomed into an array of random, potent herbs. One result is morrowgrain, a mysterious herb we know little about; I very much hope to unravel this mystery for the Circle.\nTake this voucher over to my daughter Bashana, and she will give you some seeds so you may assist us. If you run out, you will need to purchase more from her.","rew":"You will receive:\n20 Packet of Tharlendris Seeds\nExperience: 470\n+10 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Peace and serenity be yours, friend. You are here on business from the Arch Druid himself, yes?","done":"Yes, this voucher is good for twenty packets of seeds. If you run out, we have more that can be provided. Unfortunately though, Tharlendris seeds are quite costly to produce in significant numbers. This is why the Cenarion Circle asks that those who are assisting us help out by offsetting some of the cost.\nThose who return with morrowgrain find that the reward the Arch Druid offers far makes up for the cost.","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":78.6,"y":28.6,"n":"Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":71.1,"y":34.2,"n":"Bashana Runetotem","e":1}],"cats":["thunder-bluff"]},"99142":{"id":99142,"t":"Tomb weed","lv":11,"min":5,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect 5 Tomb Weed and deliver them back to Junior Apothecary Holland.\n5 Tomb Weed","desc":"If you're heading east, towards the Balnir Farmstead, I have more you might do for me. Good help is ever so hard to find these days, as your run-in with Gordo illuminates ever so clearly.\nAs I acquire doom weed I perform some minor alchemical alterations and replant them on that farmstead to cultivate my ultimate creation. I call it tomb weed, and it shall be the herald of my glorious destiny.\nDo keep an eye on the Scourge in the area while you're there. They seem... drawn... to the weed. Curious.","back":"More interruptions! Wait, it's you. Were you able to recover the tomb weed?","done":"Most glorious indeed!\n<Junior Apothecary Holland inspects the weeds.>\nHmm, I had hoped they would have matured a bit more violently. Nevertheless, progress is progress!\nA great many will die as a result of your actions this day. You should be proud.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":57.6,"y":49,"n":"Junior Apothecary Holland","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"2342":{"id":2342,"t":"Reclaimed Treasures","lv":43,"min":33,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Get Patrick Garrett's family treasure from their family chest in the South Common Hall of Uldaman, and bring it to him in the Undercity.\nGarrett Family Treasure Garrett Family Chest","desc":"Sweeping the bat pens with this broom is not befitting a Garrett! I've earned a little coin from this accursed job, and I'm willing to spend it on you to better my station.\nThe Garrett family weapon of choice is locked away in our chest in the South Common Hall of Uldaman from when we Garretts toiled there as diggers. Without it, I will be stuck here forever - literally - sweeping up after these infernal bats.\nReclaim my family's treasure and bring it to me! Help me restore my birthright!","rew":"Money: 60 0 gold, 60 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,600\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"The sweeping never ends... these bats are prolific in their mockery of me and my broom. Please tell me you've reclaimed my family's treasure! I've offered you my silver - is that not enough?!","done":"At last - a broom worthy of a Garrett. You're bloody well worth every silver I spent on you, I say!\nDo you hear me, foul bats? I now wield the Garrett family weapon of choice! Tremble, bats, tremble!!\nUndercity Loch Modan","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":62.3,"y":48.6,"n":"Patrick Garrett","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["uldaman"]},"3942":{"id":3942,"t":"Linken's Memory","lv":54,"min":47,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Eridan Bluewind in southern Felwood.","desc":"Oh... Linken? Yeah, he's a funny one. When he first got here, he was mumbling about all kinds of strange things. Probably got bumped on the head pretty hard, I imagine.\nSomething he said kinda stuck with me though -- that he was making some sort of totem; said he had to talk to someone named Eridan Bluewind... in a place called Felwood, I think?\nI doubt he could tell you much now, though. If you want to know more, maybe you should look for Eridan yourself?","rew":"Experience: 5,450","done":"Hello, ‹class›. Is there something I can help you with?\nUn'Goro Crater Felwood","pins":[{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":41.9,"y":2.7,"n":"J.D. Collie","s":1},{"z":"Felwood","x":51.3,"y":81.5,"n":"Eridan Bluewind","e":1}],"cats":["ungoro-crater"]},"4502":{"id":4502,"t":"Volcanic Activity","lv":55,"min":49,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Collect 9 samples of Un'Goro Ash from the fire elementals around the volcano in Un'Goro Crater, and return them to Liv Rizzlefix in Ratchet.\n9 Un'Goro Ash Scorching Elemental , Living Blaze , Blazerunner , Blazing Invader and 1 more","desc":"Being an apprentice to Marvon Rivetseeker, I've learned so much. But he's been gone for such a long time now, so I think I'm going to work on some experiments of my own.\nI've been reading about Un'Goro Crater most recently, and about the strange volcanic activity going on in the middle of the crater. I think a lot could be learned if I could just get some of the ash from the elementals there.\nDo you think you'd mind collecting some for me, if you are going that way?","rew":"Money: 85 0 gold, 85 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,650\n+100 reputation with Ratchet","back":"Is it true that the volcano in Un'Goro is active? I'm sure I could learn a lot with some ash from the volcano, ‹name›.","done":"These samples will be perfect for my studies! Thank you, ‹name›! I promise, you'll be the first one I will tell about my findings.\nThe Barrens Un'Goro Crater","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.4,"y":38.7,"n":"Liv Rizzlefix","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ungoro-crater"]},"8422":{"id":8422,"t":"Trolls of a Feather","lv":52,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a total of 6 Voodoo Feathers from the trolls in sunken temple.\n2 Amber Voodoo Feather Gasher , Zul'Lor\n2 Blue Voodoo Feather Hukku , Mijan\n2 Green Voodoo Feather Zolo , Loro","desc":"My pet is almost done. Now I just need something to stuff it with.\nOnly the voodoo feathers from the trolls in the sunken temple will do. They go by the names Gasher, Mijan, Zolo, Hukku, Zul'lor, and Loro. Kill them. Kill them all.\nThis is no trivial task ‹name›, so I'll make it worth your while by giving you something of Niby's -- he probably doesn't need it anyhow.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSoul Harvester Abyss Shard Robes of Servitude\nMoney: 1 55 1 gold, 55 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,350","back":"Did you bring the feathers? This doll needs stuffed!","done":"Wonderful, now my pet is complete!\n<Impsy quickly stuffs the doll and gives it a demonic hug.>\nOh, what an odd side effect these voodoo feathers have...","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":41.5,"y":45,"n":"Impsy","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"1702":{"id":1702,"t":"The Shieldsmith","lv":22,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Cask of Scalder to Furen Longbeard.\nCask of Scalder\nProvided: Cask of Scalder","desc":"You really showed what you were made of when you ran the Rethban Gauntlet, ‹name›. And I'm true to my word. I'll get you the reward I promised...\nExcept it's in Stormwind.\nTalk to my friend, Furen Longbeard, in the Dwarven District of Stormwind. He's the best shieldsmith you'll ever meet, and he owes me a big favor.\nHere, take Furen this cask of Barleybrew Scalder and ask him for a shield. He'll give you a nice one.","rew":"You will receive:\nFuren's Favor\nExperience: 440","back":"Hello! Dry times, don't you think?","done":"Ah, Barleybrew Scalder. Great stuff! So you've been to see Yorus, eh?\nI can get you a shield, yes sir/ma'am! You won't find a better one, and that's no lying!\nRedridge Mountains Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":21.5,"y":44.7,"n":"Yorus Barleybrew","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":64.6,"y":37.2,"n":"Furen Longbeard","e":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"1782":{"id":1782,"t":"Furen's Armor","lv":28,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nFire Hardened Hauberk\nExperience: 3,400","done":"Here's your armor, ‹name›. This will stand up to the strongest assaults or my name isn't Furen Longbeard!\nAnd I have to thank you. I learned a lot while working with the materials\nyou brought me. I think I'll have another breakthrough one day!\nI'm going to send what I learned to other\nblacksmiths of the Alliance.\nI'll tell them you were a big help, and maybe they'll want to return the favor.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":64.6,"y":37.2,"n":"Furen Longbeard","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"5222":{"id":5222,"t":"Target: Writhing Haunt","lv":55,"min":50,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Go to the Writhing Haunt in Western Plaguelands to locate and defeat the Cauldron Lord present there, and use its key to gain access to the cauldron. You must have the Empty Writhing Haunt Bottle with you to secure a sample of the poisons used inside the cauldron.\nWrithing Haunt Cauldron Key Cauldron Lord Razarch\nEmpty Writhing Haunt Bottle\nProvided: Empty Writhing Haunt Bottle","desc":"Two cauldrons have been successfully opened; while you will be able to access them indefinitely, we still want to open up the other two that remain. This will provide all of us with more options to introduce the counter agent!\nThis time, you'll be hitting the Writhing Haunt's cauldron. It is almost due east of Andorhal, relatively close to the ruined city walls; again, eliminate the cauldron lord present there for its key. Use this bottle to obtain the sample from the cauldron.\nGood hunting, ‹name›!","rew":"Experience: 5,650\n+100 reputation with Stormwind\n+100 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"An access panel to the cauldron remains securely fastened. In order to open it, you will need to find the key.","done":"The cauldron lord's key unlocks the access panel to this cauldron and then disappears, much like the other keys have for the previous two cauldrons you've dealt of. A putrid smelling substance churns violently beneath the platform of the cauldron.\nThere is a small spigot that the bottle fits well enough under, allowing you to draw a sample for High Priestess MacDonnell back at Chillwind Point.","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":43,"y":84.5,"n":"High Priestess MacDonnell","s":1},{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":53,"y":65.6,"n":"Scourge Cauldron","e":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"5862":{"id":5862,"t":"Scarlet Subterfuge","lv":60,"min":52,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Myranda to gain the Scarlet Illusion. Travel to Hearthglen while under the Scarlet Illusion and deliver Tirion's Gift to Highlord Taelan Fordring.\nHearthglen is to the north, Taelan should be inside of Mardenholde Keep.\nTirion's Gift\nProvided: Tirion's Gift","desc":"I am what you would call, an illusionist. Though I may be able to create an illusion to allow you entry into Hearthglen, be warned; my powers have their limitations.\nShould you travel too far from these lands, the effects of the illusion will cease. The spell itself takes a great amount of concentration and power from me, and thus, I can only sustain the effect for a short time.\nSpeak to me again when you are ready.","rew":"Experience: 6,600","back":"Are you the reinforcements from Tyr's Hand?","done":"What is this, soldier?\n<Taelan opens the box and begins to examine its contents.>\nThis... this cannot be true. But all that you have shown me...\n<Taelan falls to one knee, his heartbeat quickens. The fury of ages is about to be loosed upon this town.>","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":50.8,"y":77.8,"n":"Myranda the Hag","s":1},{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":42,"y":14.8,"n":"Highlord Taelan Fordring","e":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"5462":{"id":5462,"t":"The Dying, Ras Frostwhisper","lv":60,"min":57,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Light's Hope in Eastern Plaguelands and seek out Leonid Barthalomew the Revered. Show him the Keepsake of Remembrance and tell him all that you have discovered.\nKeepsake of Remembrance Keepsake of Remembrance\nProvided: Keepsake of Remembrance","desc":"Upon tainted soil, the keepsake must be attuned.\nIt is rumored that Stratholme is where Frostwhisper succumbed to the Lich King. Upon those bloodied grounds he gave his life - freely and with motive - to become one of the undying.\nIt is those grounds that must be found.\nThere is one, an undead dissenter of the Scourge, freed by the Banshee Queen but loyal to the cause of the Argent Dawn. Find him: Leonid Barthalomew the Revered. He may know more. Seek out Light's Hope, ‹name›.","rew":"Experience: 4,950","back":"Do not ask questions of which you do not want answers.","done":"<Leonid looks over the keepsake.>\nYour quandary stirs up memories that I had hoped would never resurface.\nWestern Plaguelands Eastern Plaguelands","pins":[{"z":"Western Plaguelands","x":70.6,"y":74.1,"n":"Magistrate Marduke","s":1},{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.9,"y":48.3,"n":"Leonid Barthalomew the Revered","e":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"22":{"id":22,"t":"Goretusk Liver Pie","lv":12,"min":9,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Salma Saldean needs 8 Goretusk livers to make a Goretusk Liver Pie.\n8 Goretusk Liver Bellygrub 37.7 % , Great Goretusk 37 % , Goretusk 33 % , Young Goretusk 32.4 %","desc":"The onions are peeled. The garlic is minced. The rosemary is crushed. The crust has been baked. The dill weed is chopped. The gravy is simmering. Now all I need for my famous meat pie are 8 Goretusk Livers!","rew":"You will receive:\n3 Goretusk Liver Pie Recipe: Goretusk Liver Pie\nExperience: 900\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"All I need for my famous meat pie are 8 Goretusk Livers!","done":"These are just perfect, ‹name›! Thank you so much. Farmer Saldean and I are going to feast tonight. And here is a little something for you, for the hard work. You didn't think I was going to let a ‹class› like you go hungry, did you?","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":56.4,"y":30.5,"n":"Salma Saldean","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"92742":{"id":92742,"t":"Testing the wells","lv":12,"min":9,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Use the Well Water Sample Kit to collect samples from the wells at the Jansen Stead and the Molsen Farm.\nJansen Stead Water Sample\nMolsen Farm Water Sample\nProvided: Well Water Sample Kit","desc":"We must determine the source and nature of the poison corrupting this land. Let us begin with the groundwater under the farms in the area.\nGo to the Jansen Stead and the Molsen Farm, and collect samples from the wells there.","rew":"Money: 2 50 0 gold, 2 silver, 50 copper Experience: 460\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Did you collect the samples?","done":"Thank you. Let me see...","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":52.4,"y":53,"n":"Alba Fairmoon","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"102":{"id":102,"t":"Patrolling Westfall","lv":14,"min":8,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 8 Gnoll Paws to Captain Danuvin on Sentinel Hill.\n8 Gnoll Paw Sergeant Brashclaw 80 % , Riverpaw Miner 80 % , Riverpaw Shaman 80 % , Riverpaw Herbalist 80 % and 4 more","desc":"Stormwind has abandoned us. A foul wind of depravity rustles through the plains of Westfall. This was my homeland and I will not turn my back on the citizens who choose to remain here. We, the former farmers, shall make our stand.\nYour task, should you choose to accept, is to patrol the grasslands of Westfall. Track down and slay the vile Gnolls that seem to be working in conjunction with the Deadmines thieves. Bring me eight Gnoll Paws and I will reward your bravery.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBelt of the People's Militia Bracers of the People's Militia\nExperience: 975\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Have you collected 8 paws from those treacherous Gnolls yet?","done":"Well done, ‹name›. With valiant adventurers such as yourself fighting alongside The People's Militia, Westfall just might return to the prosperous breadbasket it once was. Please accept this in recognition of your tireless efforts.","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":56.4,"y":47.6,"n":"Captain Danuvin","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"1302":{"id":1302,"t":"James Hyal","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Clerk Lendry at Foothold Citadel in Theramore.","desc":"My brother James went with Lady Proudmoore across the sea. Last I heard, the fighting had settled down over there, and James was setting up an inn somewhere on the continent. Wherever he is, I'm sure he's doing good business. Damn fine cook he was.\nI haven't heard from him for a while now--too busy with his inn, I'd wager--but the clerk in Theramore could probably point you to him. Look for him on the top floor of that keep near the middle of the city. What's it called... Foothold Citadel, that's it.","rew":"Experience: 700","done":"James Hyal, James Hyal... Why does that name sound so familiar?\nOf course! The Shady Rest Inn incident. If you have any information about what happened there, I would urge you to speak with Captain Vimes about it. He's handling the investigation.\nWetlands Dustwallow Marsh","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":8.4,"y":61.8,"n":"Vincent Hyal","s":1},{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":67.9,"y":48.2,"n":"Clerk Lendry","e":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"4902":{"id":4902,"t":"Wildkin of Elune","lv":57,"min":52,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm in Darnassus.","desc":"That's fascinating!\nI have always wondered about the truth... Well, you must share this knowledge, definitely! Go to Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm right away -- you'll find him in Darnassus, in the Cenarion Circle. Explain to him what happened, just the same as you told me. I'm sure he will be just as interested!\nThis is important information, ‹name›!","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nThornflinger Opaline Medallion\nExperience: 6,000\n+100 reputation with Alliance","done":"Do not hesitate; tell me why you have come.\nOh, yes? Hmm. Well.\nThank you for bringing this straight to me; it is always best to go right to the top... But... Yes. The druids of the Cenarion Circle have known of the Wildkin for some time. That they are pets of Elune, and were chosen to guard the most sacred of places.\nSo while this isn't news, I definitely compliment you on your effort. Here, take this -- it is something that seems suitable for such a deed.\nTeldrassil Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":55.5,"y":92,"n":"Erelas Ambersky","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":34.8,"y":9.3,"n":"Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm","e":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"94902":{"id":94902,"t":"Valanaar vintages","lv":11,"min":8,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect $1oa grapes.","desc":"[PH] Collect grapes from the vineyard\nLevel 11 , requires level 8 Difficulty 8 9 14 17 Side Both factions Shareable Yes Quest ID 94902","cats":["zephras-isle"]},"8102":{"id":8102,"t":"The Pebble of Kajaro","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60.","obj":"Pebble of Kajaro","rew":"You will receive:\nPebble of Kajaro\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"Welcome back, ‹class›. I can see that the pebble has seen much use. Many of our foes have fallen to your otherworldly abilities. Their suffering has been great. It is time that I enhance the power of the pebble. Give it to me.","done":"Be unstoppable, like the molten fronts of Kajaro.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.3,"y":16.1,"n":"Al'tabim the All-Seeing","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zulgurub"]}});